CET.data.listeningByYear[2024] = [{"id":"L11","level":"CET6","type":"长对话","source":"2024年6月 · 六级 · 长对话","year":2024,"session":"6月","title":"学术会议的行程","intro":"助理与教授核对学术会议的日程冲突，并安排机票、住宿与材料。","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet6-2024-06-set1.mp3","lines":[{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Thank you for meeting with me, Stephen, at such short notice.","cn":"W: 谢谢你在这么短的时间内抽空见我，Stephen。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Not a problem, Margaret.","cn":"M: 没问题，Margaret。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Now, please give me some good news.","cn":"现在，请告诉我一些好消息。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Have you agreed to my last proposal?","cn":"你同意我上次的提议了吗？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: I have, indeed.","cn":"W: 确实同意了。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"And I wish to sign the agreement pending one small change to be made to the contract.","cn":"我希望签署协议，前提是对合同做一处小改动。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Margaret, we've been through this for almost a year now, back and forth, making alterations.","cn":"M: Margaret，我们为这件事来回磋商、不断修改，已经快一年了。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Are you sure you want to make a sponsorship deal for your clients, or not?","cn":"你到底确定要为你的客户达成一项赞助协议，还是不想？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"I ask this, because, frankly, some people at my end are running out of patience.","cn":"我之所以这样问，是因为坦率地说，我这边有些人已经快失去耐心了。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: I understand your concerns.","cn":"W: 我理解你的担忧。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"But as I'm sure you understand, we hold our clients' best interests to be of the utmost concern.","cn":"不过，我相信你也明白，我们最关心的是客户的最大利益。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"We therefore comb through the fine details of all contracts, rest assured, we all appreciate your firm's patience.","cn":"因此，我们会仔细审阅所有合同的细节，请放心，我们都很感谢贵公司的耐心。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: OK, fine.","cn":"M: 好吧，没问题。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"So what change do you wish to make?","cn":"那么你想做什么改动？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Essentially, we would like the new deal to exclude the Middle East.","cn":"W: 基本上，我们希望新协议不包括中东地区。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"That's all.","cn":"就这些。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: The Middle East?","cn":"M: 中东地区？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Why?","cn":"为什么？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: My client has a couple of other prospective marketing deals from companies in the Middle East.","cn":"W: 我的客户还收到几家中东公司的其他潜在营销合作邀约。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Those offers, should they materialize, would exclusively employ my client's image in the Middle East only.","cn":"如果这些邀约最终落实，对方将只在中东地区使用我客户的形象。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Therefore, in order to avoid any conflict, we would need to ensure that both marketing campaigns do not overlap geographically.","cn":"因此，为了避免任何冲突，我们需要确保这两项营销活动在地域上不会重叠。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: What business sector in the Middle East are we talking about here?","cn":"M: 你说的中东业务具体属于哪个行业？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Real estate.","cn":"W: 房地产。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Well, that should be okay then.","cn":"M: 那应该没问题。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"So long as the product is very different from our food and beverage market, there should be no conflict of interest.","cn":"只要产品与我们的食品和饮料市场有很大不同，就不应存在利益冲突。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Nevertheless, I will have to run this through my people.","cn":"不过，我还是得把这件事拿去和我的团队确认一下。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"I don't foresee any problem, though.","cn":"但我预计不会有什么问题。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"The Middle East is a negligible market for us, but I still need to check this with a couple of departments.","cn":"中东对我们来说是个微不足道的市场，不过我仍然需要和几个部门核实一下。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Next, we have a special science-related news story.","cn":"M：接下来是一则特别的科学新闻报道。丹佛天文台的 Paula Hancocks，Paula，那边有什么重大新闻？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Paula Hancocks at the Denver Observatory.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Paula, what is the big story over there?","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Hi, John.","cn":"W：你好，John。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Yes, all the astronomers on site here are very excited.","cn":"是的，这里的所有天文学家都非常兴奋。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"In fact, space enthusiasts all across North America and the rest of the Northern Hemisphere will be congregating on mountain tops tonight to watch the night's sky.","cn":"事实上，整个北美以及北半球其他地区的太空爱好者今晚都会聚集到山顶，观看夜空。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Why?","cn":"M：为什么？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"What's the big event?","cn":"有什么重大事件？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Is there an eclipse happening soon?","cn":"很快要发生日食了吗？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Tonight, the Earth will come into close proximity with the Oppenheimer comet.","cn":"W：今晚，地球将与 Oppenheimer 彗星近距离接近。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"It is the closest our planet has been to such a phenomenon in over 100 years.","cn":"这是100多年来我们的星球距离此类现象最近的一次。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"For this reason, it is expected that thousands of people will gaze up at the sky tonight in order to see this formidable object.","cn":"因此，预计今晚会有数千人仰望天空，观看这个令人震撼的天体。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: How far away is this comet?","cn":"M：这颗彗星距离我们有多远？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Will people be able to see it with the naked eye?","cn":"人们用肉眼能看到它吗？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: The Oppenheimer comet will still be millions of miles away, on the edge of our galaxy.","cn":"W：Oppenheimer 彗星仍会位于数百万英里之外，在我们银河系的边缘。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But nevertheless, this is a relatively close distance, close enough for people to observe in good detail through a telescope.","cn":"不过，这仍然算是相对较近的距离，近到人们可以通过望远镜清楚地观测它。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"People will only see a blur without one.","cn":"没有望远镜的话，人们只能看到一团模糊的影像。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"However, that does not mean one needs professional equipment.","cn":"不过，这并不意味着必须使用专业设备。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Even the most ordinary of telescopes should be conducive for people to observe and wonder at this flying object.","cn":"即使是最普通的望远镜，也足以让人们观测并惊叹于这个飞行中的天体。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Many of our viewers will be wondering how they too can take part in this once-in-a-lifetime event.","cn":"M：我们的许多观众都会想知道，他们怎样才能参与这场一生难遇的活动。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Where will this comet be in the sky?","cn":"这颗彗星会出现在天空的什么位置？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"How can people find it?","cn":"人们该如何找到它？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: The comet will be almost exactly due north, at 60 degrees above the equator.","cn":"W：这颗彗星几乎正好位于正北方，在赤道上方60度的位置。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"However, finding the comet is indeed very tricky.","cn":"不过，找到这颗彗星确实非常困难。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"And scientists here have told me there are plenty of phone apps that will facilitate this.","cn":"这里的科学家告诉我，有很多手机应用可以帮助大家定位。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: How fantastic!","cn":"M：太棒了！"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Thank you, Paula, for the information.","cn":"Paula，感谢你提供这些信息。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Dietary guidelines form the basis for nutrition advice and regulations around the world.","cn":"膳食指南构成了世界各地营养建议和相关法规的基础。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"While there is strong scientific consensus around most existing guidelines, one question has recently stirred debate: should consumers be warned to avoid ultra-processed foods?","cn":"尽管现有大多数指南背后都有强有力的科学共识，但最近有一个问题引发了争议：是否应当提醒消费者避免食用超加工食品？"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Two papers published today in the American Journal of Clinical Nutrition outline the case for and against using the concept of ultra-processed foods to help inform dietary guidelines beyond conventional food classification systems.","cn":"今天发表在《美国临床营养学杂志》上的两篇论文，分别阐述了支持和反对使用“超加工食品”这一概念的理由，以帮助在传统食品分类体系之外进一步制定膳食指南。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"The authors, Carlos Monteiro of the University of São Paulo and Arne Astrup of Novo Nordisk Foundation, will discuss the issue in a live virtual debate August 14th during NUTRITION 2024 LIVE ONLINE.","cn":"论文作者、圣保罗大学的Carlos Monteiro和Novo Nordisk Foundation的Arne Astrup，将于8月14日在NUTRITION 2024 LIVE ONLINE期间举行的线上直播辩论中讨论这一问题。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"The debate centers around a system developed by Monteiro and colleagues that classifies foods by their degree of industrial processing, ranging from unprocessed to ultra-processed.","cn":"这场辩论围绕Monteiro及其同事制定的一套体系展开，该体系根据食品的工业加工程度对其进行分类，范围从未加工食品到超加工食品。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"The system defines ultra-processed foods as those made using sequences of processes that extract substances from foods and alter them with chemicals in order to formulate the final product.","cn":"该体系将超加工食品定义为：通过一系列加工步骤制成的食品，在这些步骤中，先从食品中提取物质，再使用化学品对其进行改变，以配制出最终产品。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Ultra-processed foods are characteristically designed to be cheap, tasty, and convenient; examples include soft drinks and candy, packaged snacks and pastries, ready-to-heat products, and reconstituted meat products.","cn":"超加工食品通常被设计成价格低廉、美味可口且方便食用；其中包括软饮料和糖果、包装零食和糕点、即热食品以及再制肉制品等。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Studies have linked consumption of ultra-processed foods—which are packed high in salt, sugar, and fat—with weight gain and an increased risk of chronic diseases, even after adjusting for the amount of salt, sugar, and fat in the diet.","cn":"研究表明，食用超加工食品会导致体重增加并提高患慢性疾病的风险；这类食品含有大量盐、糖和脂肪，即使在对膳食中盐、糖和脂肪的含量进行调整后，这些关联仍然存在。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"While the mechanisms behind these associations are not fully understood, Monteiro argues that the existing evidence is sufficient to justify discouraging consumption of ultra-processed foods in dietary recommendations and government policies.","cn":"尽管这些关联背后的机制尚未被完全理解，Monteiro认为，现有证据已经足以支持在膳食建议和政府政策中劝阻人们食用超加工食品。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Believe it or not, human creativity benefits from constraints.","cn":"信不信由你，限制有益于人类的创造力。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"According to psychologists, when you have less to work with, you actually begin to see the world differently.","cn":"心理学家认为，当你可利用的资源较少时，你实际上会开始以不同的方式看待世界。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"With constraints, you dedicate your mental energy to acting more resourcefully.","cn":"有了限制，你会将 mental energy 投入到更具资源性地采取行动上。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"When challenged, you figure out new ways to be better.","cn":"面对挑战时，你会想出新的方法，让自己做得更好。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The most successful creative people know that constraints give their minds the impetus to leap higher.","cn":"最成功的创意人士知道，限制会促使他们的思维跃得更高。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"People who invent new products are not limited by what they don't have or can't do.","cn":"发明新产品的人不会受到自己没有什么或不能做什么的限制。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"They leverage their limitations to push themselves even further.","cn":"他们利用自身的局限，推动自己更进一步。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Many products and services are created because the founders saw a limitation in what they use.","cn":"许多产品和服务之所以诞生，是因为创始人发现自己所使用的产品或服务存在局限。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"They created innovation based on what was not working for them at the moment.","cn":"他们根据当时对自己不起作用的地方创造了创新。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Innovation is a creative person's response to limitation.","cn":"创新是创意人士对局限的回应。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"In a 2015 study which examined how thinking about scarcity or abundance influences how creatively people use their resources, Ravi Mehta at the University of Illinois and Meng Zhu at Johns Hopkins University found that people simply have no incentive to use what's available to them in novel ways.","cn":"在一项于2015年开展的研究中，伊利诺伊大学的Ravi Mehta和约翰斯·霍普金斯大学的Meng Zhu考察了对稀缺或富足的思考如何影响人们创造性地使用资源，并发现人们根本没有动力以新颖的方式利用手头的资源。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"When people face scarcity, they give themselves the freedom to use resources in less conventional ways because they have to.","cn":"当人们面临资源稀缺时，他们会迫使自己以不那么传统的方式使用资源，因为他们不得不这样做。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Obstacles can broaden your perception and open up your thinking processes.","cn":"障碍可以拓宽你的认知，并开启你的思维过程。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Consistent constraints help you improve at connecting unrelated ideas and concepts.","cn":"持续存在的限制有助于你提高将不相关的想法和概念联系起来的能力。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Marissa Mayer, former vice president for search products and user experience at Google, once wrote in a publication on Bloomberg, \"Constraints shape and focus problems and provide clear challenges to overcome; Creativity thrives best when constrained.\"","cn":"谷歌前搜索产品和用户体验副总裁Marissa Mayer曾在彭博社的一篇刊物中写道：“限制能够塑造问题、聚焦问题，并提供有待克服的明确挑战；创造力在受到限制时最能蓬勃发展。”"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Different people use different strategies for managing conflicts.","cn":"不同的人会采用不同的冲突处理策略。这些策略是在童年时期学会的。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"These strategies are learned in childhood.","cn":"通常，我们并没有意识到自己在冲突情境中是如何行动的，只是按照看似自然而然的方式去做。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Usually, we are not aware of how we act in conflict situations.","cn":"但我们确实都有自己的策略，而且由于这种策略是后天习得的，所以我们始终可以通过学习新的、更有效的冲突处理方式来改变它。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"We just do whatever seems to come naturally.","cn":"当你卷入冲突时，有两个主要方面需要考虑：实现个人目标，以及与对方保持良好关系。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"But we do have a personal strategy, and because it is learned, we can always change it by learning new and more effective ways of managing conflicts.","cn":"个人目标对你的重要程度，以及这段关系对你的重要程度，都会影响你在冲突中的行为。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"When you get involved in a conflict, there are two major concerns you have to take into account: achieving your personal goals and keeping a good relationship with the other person.","cn":"根据这两个方面，可以确定五种冲突处理风格。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"How important your personal goals are and how important the relationship is to you affect how you act in a conflict.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Given these two concerns, five styles of managing conflicts can be identified.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The turtle.","cn":"龟型。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Turtles withdraw into their shells to avoid conflicts.","cn":"乌龟会缩进壳里以避免冲突。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They give up their personal goals and relationships.","cn":"它们放弃个人目标和人际关系。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They believe it is easier to withdraw from a conflict than to face it.","cn":"它们认为，与其面对冲突，不如退出冲突更容易。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The shark.","cn":"鲨鱼型。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Sharks try to overpower opponents by forcing them to accept their solution to the conflict.","cn":"鲨鱼试图迫使对方接受自己提出的冲突解决方案，从而压倒对方。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They seek to achieve their goals at all costs.","cn":"它们不惜一切代价追求实现自己的目标。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Sharks assume that conflicts are settled by one person winning and one person losing.","cn":"鲨鱼认为，冲突的解决方式是一方获胜、另一方失败。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Winning gives sharks a sense of pride and achievement.","cn":"获胜会让鲨鱼产生自豪感和成就感；"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Losing gives them a sense of weakness, inadequacy, and failure.","cn":"失败则会让它们感到软弱、无能和挫败。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The teddy bear.","cn":"泰迪熊型。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Teddy bears want to be accepted and liked by other people.","cn":"泰迪熊希望得到他人的接纳和喜爱。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They think that conflict should be avoided in favor of harmony, and believe that conflicts cannot be discussed without damaging relationships.","cn":"它们认为，为了保持和谐，应当避免冲突，并相信讨论冲突会损害人际关系。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They give up their goals to preserve the relationship.","cn":"它们放弃自己的目标，以维护这段关系。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The fox.","cn":"狐狸型。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Foxes are moderately concerned with their own goals and about their relationships with other people.","cn":"狐狸对自身目标以及与他人的关系都抱有适度的关注。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They give up part of their goals and persuade the other person in a conflict to give up part of his goals.","cn":"它们放弃一部分自己的目标，并说服冲突中的对方也放弃一部分目标。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They seek a solution to conflicts where both sides gain something.","cn":"它们寻求一种能让双方都获得一些利益的冲突解决方案。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The owl.","cn":"猫头鹰型。猫头鹰把冲突视为需要解决的问题。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Owls view conflicts as problems to be solved.","cn":"它们认为，冲突能够通过减少两个人之间的紧张关系来改善人际关系。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They see conflicts as improving relationships by reducing tension between two people.","cn":"它们试图展开讨论，将冲突界定为一个问题。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They try to begin a discussion that identifies the conflict as a problem.","cn":"通过寻求既能满足自己又能满足对方的解决方案，猫头鹰得以维持这段关系。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"By seeking solutions that satisfy both themselves and the other person, owls maintain the relationship.","cn":"在找到既能实现自己的目标、又能实现对方目标的解决方案之前，猫头鹰不会感到满意；"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Owls are not satisfied until a solution is found that achieves their own goals and the other person's goals, and they are not satisfied until the tensions and negative feelings have been fully resolved.","cn":"在紧张情绪和负面感受得到彻底解决之前，它们也不会感到满意。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The genetic code of all 1.5 million known species of animals and plants living on earth will be mapped to help save species from extinction and boost human health.","cn":"地球上现存的全部150万种已知动植物的遗传密码将被测序，以帮助拯救濒临灭绝的物种并促进人类健康。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Scientists hope that cracking the genetic code of plants and animals could help uncover new treatments for infectious diseases, slow aging, improve crops in agriculture, and create new bio-materials.","cn":"科学家希望，破解动植物的遗传密码能够帮助发现传染病的新疗法、延缓衰老、改良农业作物，并创造新的生物材料。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"In Britain, organizations including the Natural History Museum, the Royal Botanic Gardens at Kew and the Wellcome Sanger Institute have joined forces to sequence Britain's 66,000 species of animals and plants.","cn":"在英国，包括自然历史博物馆、邱园皇家植物园和Wellcome Sanger研究所在内的多个组织已经联合起来，为英国的6.6万种动植物进行基因测序。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Dubbed the Darwin Tree of Life Project, it is expected to take 10 years and cost £100 million.","cn":"该项目被称为“达尔文生命之树项目”，预计将耗时10年，耗资1亿英镑。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Once completed, all the information will be publicly available to researchers.","cn":"项目完成后，所有信息都将向研究人员公开。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Many scientists believe that earth has now entered the sixth mass extinction, with humans creating a toxic mix of habitat loss, pollution and climate change, which has already led to the loss of at least 77 species of mammals and 140 types of birds since 1500.","cn":"许多科学家认为，地球如今已经进入第六次大灭绝时期，人类造成的栖息地丧失、污染和气候变化的有害结合，已经导致自1500年以来至少77种哺乳动物和140种鸟类灭绝。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"It is the biggest loss of species since the dinosaurs were wiped out 66 million years ago.","cn":"这是自6600万年前恐龙灭绝以来最大规模的物种损失。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Scientists say that sequencing every species will revolutionise the understanding of biology and evolution, bolster efforts to conserve as well as protect and restore biodiversity.","cn":"科学家表示，对每一个物种进行测序将彻底改变人们对生物学和进化的认识，加强保护以及维护和恢复生物多样性的努力。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Dr. Tim Littlewood, head of Life Sciences Department at the Natural History Museum, said, \"Whether you are interested in food or disease, the history of how every organism on the planet has adapted to its environment is recorded in its genetic makeup.","cn":"自然历史博物馆生命科学部负责人蒂姆·利特尔伍德博士说：“无论你对食物还是疾病感兴趣，地球上每一种生物如何适应其环境的历史，都记录在它的遗传构成中。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"How you then harness that is dependent on your ability to understand it.","cn":"你如何利用这些信息，取决于你理解它的能力。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"We will be using modern methods to get a really good window on the present and the past.","cn":"我们将运用现代方法，真正清晰地了解现在和过去。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"And of course, a window on the past gives you a prospective model on the future.\"","cn":"当然，了解过去也能为未来提供一个预测模型。”"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Sir Jim Smith, Director of Science at Wellcome, said, \"Try as I might, I can't think of a more exciting, more relevant, more timely or more internationally inspirational project.","cn":"Wellcome科学部主任吉姆·史密斯爵士说：“尽管我努力思考，也想不出还有哪个项目比这更加令人兴奋、更加贴近现实、更加及时，或更能激发国际社会的灵感。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Since 1970, humanity has wiped out 60 percent of animal populations.","cn":"自1970年以来，人类已经使动物种群数量减少了60%。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"About 23,000 of 80,000 species surveyed are approaching extinction.","cn":"在接受调查的8万种物种中，约有2.3万种正走向灭绝。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"We are in the midst of the sixth great extinction event of life on our planet, which not only threatens wildlife species, but also imperils the global food supply.","cn":"我们正处于地球生命第六次大灭绝事件之中，这不仅威胁野生动物物种，也危及全球粮食供应。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"As scientists, we all realise we desperately need to catalogue life on our fragile planet now.","cn":"作为科学家，我们都意识到，现在迫切需要为我们这个脆弱星球上的生命编制目录。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"I think we're making history.\"","cn":"我认为，我们正在创造历史。”"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"John Donne, the English poet, wrote in the 17th century, \"No man is an island, entire of itself; every man is a piece of the continent, a part of the main.\" Now, a British academic has claimed that human individuality is indeed just an illusion, because societies are far more interconnected at a mental, physical, and cultural level than people realise.","cn":"英国诗人约翰·多恩在17世纪写道：“没有人是一座孤岛，自成一体；每个人都是大陆的一部分，是陆地的一部分。”如今，一位英国学者声称，人的个体性确实只是一种幻觉，因为社会在心理、身体和文化层面的相互联系，远比人们意识到的更加紧密。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In his new book, The Self Delusion, Professor Tom Oliver, a researcher in the Ecology and Evolution group at the University of Reading, argues there is no such thing as \"self\", and not even our bodies are truly \"us\".","cn":"在他的新书《The Self Delusion》中，雷丁大学生态学与进化研究组的研究员汤姆·奥利弗教授认为，根本不存在所谓的“自我”，甚至连我们的身体也并不真正是“我们”。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Just as Copernicus realised the Earth is not the centre of the universe, Professor Oliver said society urgently needs a Copernican-like revolution to understand people are not detached beings but rather part of one connected identity.","cn":"正如哥白尼意识到地球并不是宇宙的中心一样，奥利弗教授说，社会迫切需要一场类似哥白尼革命的变革，以理解人并非彼此孤立的存在，而是同一个相互联系的身份的一部分。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"\"A significant milestone in the cultural evolution of human minds was the acceptance that the Earth is not the centre of the universe, the so-called Copernican Revolution,\" he writes.","cn":"他写道：“人类心智文化演化中的一个重要里程碑，是人们接受地球并不是宇宙的中心，这就是所谓的哥白尼革命。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"\"However, we have one more big myth to dispose of: that we exist as independent selves at the centre of a subjective universe.","cn":"然而，我们还需要摒弃另一个重大的神话：我们以独立自我的身份存在于主观宇宙的中心。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"You may feel as if you are an independent individual, acting autonomously in the world; that you have an unchanging inner self that persists throughout your lifetime, acting as a central anchor-point with the world changing around you.","cn":"你可能会觉得自己是一个独立的个体，在世界上自主行动；"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"This is the illusion I seek to tackle.","cn":"觉得自己拥有一个终生持续不变的内在自我，作为一个中心锚点，而世界则在你周围不断变化。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"We are intimately connected to the world around us.\"","cn":"这正是我试图应对的幻觉。我们与周围的世界有着密切的联系。”"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Professor Oliver argues there are around 37 trillion cells in the body but most have a lifespan of just a few days or weeks, so the material \"us\" is constantly changing.","cn":"奥利弗教授认为，人体内大约有37万亿个细胞，但其中大多数的寿命只有几天或几周，因此构成“我们”的物质一直在变化。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In fact, there is no part of your body that has existed for more than 10 years.","cn":"事实上，你身体的任何部分都没有存在超过10年。“由于我们的身体本质上每隔几周就会重新形成，仅凭其中的物质显然不足以解释身份持续存在的脉络。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"\"Since our bodies are essentially made anew every few weeks, the material in them alone is clearly insufficient to explain the persistent thread of an identity.\"","cn":"”"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Professor Oliver claims that individualism is actually bad for society, and only by realising we are part of a bigger entity can we solve pressing environmental and societal problems.","cn":"奥利弗教授声称，个人主义实际上不利于社会，只有意识到我们是更大实体的一部分，才能解决紧迫的环境和社会问题。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Through selfish over-consumption we are destroying the natural world and using non-renewable resources at an accelerating rate.","cn":"我们通过自私的过度消费正在摧毁自然世界，并以越来越快的速度消耗不可再生资源。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"\"We are at a critical crossroads as a species where we must rapidly reform our mindsets and behaviour to act in less selfish ways,\" he said.","cn":"他说：“作为一个物种，我们正处于关键的十字路口，必须迅速改变我们的思维方式和行为，以更加不自私的方式行事。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"\"So let's open our eyes to the hidden connections all around us.\"","cn":"因此，让我们睁开双眼，看清周围隐藏的各种联系。”"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is the problem with the program?","options":["Two sessions clash on Thursday morning","The conference was cancelled","The hotel is too far from the hall","The flight was delayed"],"answer":0,"explain":"男士说 there is a clash，自己的报告和语言测试专场都在周四上午，构成日程冲突。"},{"q":"Why does the man want the Tuesday evening flight?","options":["It is much cheaper","He wants a full night's sleep before presenting","He has another meeting on Wednesday","There are no morning flights"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文说 I would like a full night's sleep before presenting。"},{"q":"What does the man ask the woman to do?","options":["Print his slides","Rewrite the whole program","Book a taxi for each day","Buy a new projector"],"answer":0,"explain":"原文说 could you print my slides and put them in the conference folder。"}],"cloze":[{"text":"My talk and the session on language testing are both on ______ morning.","answers":["thursday"],"hint":"星期四"},{"text":"I would like a full night's ______ before presenting.","answers":["sleep"],"hint":"睡眠"},{"text":"Could you ______ my slides and put them in the conference folder?","answers":["print"],"hint":"打印"}]},{"id":"cet4-2024-06-1","level":"CET4","exam":"2024_06_1","year":2024,"month":6,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2024年6月 四级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2024年6月 CET-4 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet4-2024-06-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Six people had to move away from their home to another place after a fire broke out in a building on Main Street Saturday, officials said.","cn":"官员称,周六Main Street一栋建筑发生火灾后,六人不得不从家中搬到另一个地方。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Firefighters responded to the three-story building shortly after 1 p.m. for a reported structure fire, according to Norwalk Deputy Fire Chief Adam Markowitz.","cn":"据Norwalk消防副局长Adam Markowitz称,消防员在下午1点刚过就接到建筑物火灾报告后赶到了这栋三层建筑。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Markowitz said crews encountered heavy smoke coming from the second floor when they arrived.","cn":"Markowitz说,消防人员到达时遇到从二楼冒出的浓烟。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"A team of about 25 firefighters then spent about 25 minutes extinguishing the flames.","cn":"随后约25名消防员组成的队伍花了大约25分钟扑灭了火焰。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Officials described the structure as a mixed-use building that features commercial businesses on the first floor and residential on the second and third floors.","cn":"官员将该建筑描述为一栋混合用途建筑,一楼为商业店铺,二楼和三楼为住宅。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Town records list four apartments in the building.","cn":"城镇记录显示该建筑内有四套公寓。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Due to smoke and heat damage, the four apartments were declared uninhabitable, and the six residents had to move to another place, officials said.","cn":"官员称,由于烟雾和高温破坏,这四套公寓被宣布不适宜居住,六名居民不得不搬到另一个地方。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"No injuries were reported in connection with the fire.","cn":"没有关于火灾造成人员伤亡的报告。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The Norwalk Fire Marshal is investigating the cause and origin of the fire.","cn":"Norwalk消防局长正在调查火灾的原因和起源。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"A new study has cast doubt on historic research suggesting that the season or month of someone's birth is associated with an increased risk of certain mental health conditions.","cn":"一项新研究对历史研究提出了质疑,这些历史研究认为某人的出生季节或月份与某些心理健康状况的风险增加有关。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The study looks at symptoms of anxiety and depression among more than 70,000 older adults in Europe.","cn":"该研究调查了欧洲超过7万名老年人的焦虑和抑郁症状。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"A number of past studies have found the link between season of birth and mental health diagnoses.","cn":"过去的许多研究发现了出生季节与心理健康诊断之间的联系。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Researchers have suggested that such links could arise from various things.","cn":"研究人员认为,这种联系可能源于各种因素。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"These include nutrient intake, sun exposure, climate, and disease exposure varying across the course of the year.","cn":"这些因素包括全年不同时期的营养摄入、阳光照射、气候和疾病暴露的变化。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"However, evidence has been mixed.","cn":"然而,证据一直是混杂的。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"More recent studies have suggested that factors such as social class or economic background have more to do with these diagnoses than month of birth.","cn":"最近的研究表明,社会阶层或经济背景等因素与这些诊断的关系比出生月份更大。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Overall, the new study found no significant relationship between participants' month of birth and symptoms of depression or anxiety.","cn":"总体而言,这项新研究发现参与者的出生月份与抑郁或焦虑症状之间没有显著关系。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"There was some variability in some countries.","cn":"在一些国家存在一些变化。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"In Poland, depressive symptoms fluctuated a little depending on birth month.","cn":"在波兰,抑郁症状根据出生月份有轻微波动。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"In the Czech Republic, the same was true of anxiety symptoms.","cn":"在捷克共和国,焦虑症状也是如此。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"But on the whole, there was no systematic pattern.","cn":"但总的来说,没有系统性模式。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Genetic researchers in China have made a clone of a star police dog.","cn":"中国的遗传研究人员克隆了一只明星警犬。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The clone was born in a laboratory in Beijing in December.","cn":"该克隆犬于12月在北京的一个实验室出生。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Tests show that the clone and her mother are almost identical genetically.","cn":"测试显示,克隆犬与其母犬在基因上几乎完全相同。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The mother dog helped solve multiple murders and many other crimes.","cn":"母犬曾协助侦破多起谋杀案和许多其他犯罪案件。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The clone has already performed better than traditionally bred dogs on several tests.","cn":"克隆犬已经在多项测试中表现得优于传统繁育的犬只。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"If the clone continues to perform as well as expected, it could mean a huge reduction in the training time for police dogs, which usually takes about five years.","cn":"如果克隆犬继续按预期表现良好,这可能意味着警犬训练时间的大幅缩减,而警犬训练通常需要约五年时间。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The ultimate goal of scientists is to produce clones of talented police dogs that can be trained in months instead of years.","cn":"科学家的最终目标是培育出优秀警犬的克隆体,使其能够在数月而非数年内完成训练。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"However, this goal is not yet possible due to the current costs of the technology.","cn":"然而,由于目前该技术的成本,这一目标尚无法实现。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"This is not the first time a clone has been made of a star police dog.","cn":"这并非首次克隆明星警犬。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"In South Korea, six clones began working with the police in 2008.","cn":"在韩国,六只克隆犬于2008年开始与警方合作。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Tom, did you see the article online about the new TV series based on the book The Three Body Problem?","cn":"W: Tom，你看到网上关于根据《三体》这本书改编的新电视剧的文章了吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: A colleague mentioned the book, but I've been so busy writing my thesis that I haven't been able to read for pleasure in months.","cn":"M: 有同事提到过这本书，但我一直忙着写论文，已经好几个月没能读闲书了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Well, sounds like if you're going to read anything for fun, this is the book.","cn":"W: 听起来如果你要读点消遣的东西，就该读这本书。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's written by a Chinese science fiction writer.","cn":"它是一位中国科幻作家写的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I can't remember his name, but he's written three books in all, and The Three Body Problem is the first in the series.","cn":"我记不得他的名字了，但他一共写了三本书，《三体》是系列的第一部。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I don't want to say too much and spoil it for you, but it's definitely got some amazing technological and sociological concepts in it.","cn":"我不想说太多剧透，但里面确实有一些很棒的技术和社会学概念。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: It does sound like it would suit my taste, but if they are making a TV series based on it now, I don't know if I should read the book or watch the show first.","cn":"M: 听起来确实符合我的口味，但如果他们现在要根据它拍电视剧，我不知道该先读书还是先看剧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I think it's better to read the book first.","cn":"W: 我觉得最好先读书。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's rare for the show or movie to be better than the book.","cn":"电视剧或电影比书好的情况很少见。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And then, you just end up ruining the book for yourself, if the show isn't very good.","cn":"而且如果剧拍得不好，你就把书给毁了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: When is the show supposed to start?","cn":"M: 这个剧什么时候开播？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I'm a bit overwhelmed with the amount of data I still need to collect to finish my thesis.","cn":"我现在还有大量数据要收集才能完成论文，有点应接不暇。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But I still need to relax sometimes.","cn":"但我还是需要偶尔放松一下。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I can't remember exactly.","cn":"W: 我记不太清了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's pretty soon, and it's going to be quite long.","cn":"挺快的，而且会很长。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"There are 24 episodes.","cn":"有24集。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Well, maybe you could download an electronic copy of the book and try to read it before the show starts.","cn":"也许你可以下载电子版的书，在剧开播前试着读完。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: That's a good idea.","cn":"M: 这主意不错。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And then, maybe we can watch the series together.","cn":"然后也许我们可以一起看这部剧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Thanks for the tip, Alice.","cn":"谢谢你的建议，Alice。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: No problem.","cn":"W: 不客气。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Hello, good afternoon.","cn":"W: 你好，下午好。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I have an inquiry to make.","cn":"我有个问题想咨询一下。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's about the vegetarian food festival you are holding on the 19th of August at the Newcastle City Hall.","cn":"是关于你们8月19日在纽卡斯尔市政厅举办的素食美食节的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Yes, of course.","cn":"M: 好的，当然可以。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"My name's Philip.","cn":"我叫Philip。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"How can I help you?","cn":"有什么可以帮您的吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: It says on your website that you are still looking for vendors, and I grow organic vegetables on my farm, as well as doing my own home baking.","cn":"W: 你们网站上说还在招募摊主，我在自己的农场种植有机蔬菜，同时也自己在家烘焙。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Would I be able to sell both the vegetables and items baked from them at the festival?","cn":"我能在美食节上同时售卖蔬菜和用这些蔬菜烘焙的食品吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: That's exactly the type of thing we are looking for. We're getting close to the deadline, however. Do you prefer to fill out an application on the web, or to print it out and fill it in by hand and then post it back to us? Remember that you will have to have all your certificates to hand when you are filling out the forms, as the standards are high and they'll be carefully checked before anyone will be able to sell their produce at the event.","cn":"M: 这正是我们在寻找的。不过我们快到截止日期了。您是想在网上填写申请表，还是打印出来手工填写然后邮寄给我们?请注意，填表时您需要准备好所有的证书，因为标准很高，在任何人能够在活动上售卖产品之前，这些证书都会被仔细审核。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I should be fine with doing it on your website, and I already have all my certificates, as we run a small farm shop too.","cn":"W: 我在你们网站上填应该没问题，而且我已经有所有证书了，因为我们也经营一家小型农场商店。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But can you give me your details anyway?","cn":"不过你还是能把邮寄地址给我吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Sure.","cn":"M: 当然。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Please address it to the Organic Organization, Vendor Applications, 112 Queens Road, Newcastle, Northumbria.","cn":"请寄到Organic Organization，Vendor Applications，112 Queens Road，Newcastle，Northumbria。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"The postcode is NU 29 3LJ.","cn":"邮编是NU 29 3LJ。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Remember that the closing date is next Tuesday, the 28th of June.","cn":"请记住截止日期是下周二，6月28日。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That's absolutely wonderful.","cn":"W: 太好了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Thank you so much for your help.","cn":"非常感谢你的帮助。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Goodbye.","cn":"再见。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Supporters call it \"wild camping\"; opponents call it \"illegal camping\".","cn":"支持者称之为\"野外露营\"；反对者称之为\"非法露营\"。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"What both sides accept is that there has been a boom in the past few months, with increasing numbers of visitors pitching their tents on any bit of land they fancy in the UK.","cn":"双方都承认的是，过去几个月出现了激增现象，越来越多的游客在英国任何他们看中的土地上搭起帐篷。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"In part, this reflects the fact that official campsites have been wholly or partially closed, or are overflowing in a summer when fewer people are going abroad.","cn":"这在一定程度上反映了一个事实，即官方露营地已经全部或部分关闭，或者在这个出国人数较少的夏天已经人满为患。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It is also cheap, at a time when many are worried about what the economic future holds.","cn":"在许多人担心未来经济前景的时候，这也很便宜。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But it may also be an expression of a desire for going outdoors—a response to the months of lockdown.","cn":"但这也可能是一种对户外活动渴望的表达——一种对数月封锁的回应。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Most of the coverage of the boom in wild camping has been negative.","cn":"关于野外露营热潮的大部分报道都是负面的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Camping in public parks has now been banned for August and the early part of September because campers dump litter, human waste, and even their tents on the grassland.","cn":"由于露营者在草地上倾倒垃圾、人类排泄物甚至他们的帐篷，公共公园现已禁止在8月和9月初进行露营。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Similar action has been taken even in Scotland, where camping is usually permitted on most of its open land.","cn":"即使在苏格兰也采取了类似的行动，而那里通常允许在其大部分开放土地上露营。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Clearly there have to be rules.","cn":"显然必须有规则。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It would make sense that wild campers need to ask for permission to camp from landowners, especially outside Scotland, where the law is far more restrictive.","cn":"野外露营者需要向土地所有者征求露营许可是合理的,特别是在苏格兰以外的地区，那里的法律要严格得多。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It would be common sense for people to use small tents and leave no trace of their visit.","cn":"人们使用小帐篷并不留下任何访问痕迹是常识。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"They have been attracted by a patch of land this close to wilderness, and it is their responsibility to keep it that way.","cn":"他们被这片如此接近荒野的土地所吸引，保持其原貌是他们的责任。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Imagine boating down the Amazon River, minding your own business—calmly keeping an eye out for alarmingly large snakes—and a curious pink dolphin appears to swim alongside.","cn":"想象一下，你正在亚马逊河上划船，专心做着自己的事——平静地留意着那些大得惊人的蛇——这时一只好奇的粉红色海豚出现在你身边游动。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"While this may seem like a mythical creature, pink dolphins do exist in the Amazon region.","cn":"虽然这看起来像是神话中的生物，但粉红色海豚确实存在于亚马逊地区。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The Amazon river dolphin is a giant among its species.","cn":"亚马逊河豚是其物种中的巨型成员。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It can measure up to 2 meters long and weigh around 204 kilograms.","cn":"它的体长可达2米，体重约204千克。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Size isn't the only thing that sets the Amazon river dolphin apart.","cn":"体型并不是亚马逊河豚与众不同的唯一特征。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Thriving in South American rivers and temporary lakes caused by seasonal flooding, this freshwater dolphin is sometimes shockingly pink.","cn":"这种淡水豚栖息在南美洲的河流和季节性洪水形成的临时湖泊中，有时会呈现出令人震惊的粉红色。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Although born gray, males of the species are easily identified as they enter adulthood by a decisive pink shade.","cn":"虽然出生时是灰色的，但该物种的雄性在进入成年期后很容易通过明显的粉红色阴影来识别。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Their unusual coloring is believed to be the result of scar tissue from dolphin fights—whether playful fighting or a serious bid for a mate.","cn":"它们不寻常的颜色被认为是海豚打斗留下的疤痕组织的结果——无论是嬉戏打闹还是为争夺配偶的激烈竞争。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The deeper the pink, the more attractive the males are believed to be, and the older the male, the more pink it will have.","cn":"粉红色越深，雄性被认为越有吸引力，而雄性年龄越大，粉红色就越多。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"There's also a theory that this color helps the dolphins more readily blend in with their surroundings.","cn":"还有一种理论认为，这种颜色有助于海豚更容易地与周围环境融为一体。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"During heavy rains, rivers along the Amazon rainforest turn a pink shade, and with it male dolphins are harder to detect.","cn":"在大雨期间，亚马逊雨林沿岸的河流会呈现粉红色，雄性海豚也因此更难被发现。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The Amazon wetland system, fed by the Amazon River, is a crucial place for pink dolphins to breed, and since 2018 has been granted internationally protected status.","cn":"由亚马逊河滋养的亚马逊湿地系统是粉红色海豚繁殖的关键场所，自2018年以来已被授予国际保护地位。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"In a new Merrill Lynch/Age Wave survey, a full 70% of the early adults said they received financial support from their parents in the past year and 58% said they couldn't afford their current lifestyles without it.","cn":"在 Merrill Lynch/Age Wave 的一项新调查中，70% 的年轻成年人表示他们在过去一年中得到了父母的经济支持，58% 的人表示如果没有这些支持，他们无法负担目前的生活方式。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The most common types of financial support include cell phone plans, food, school costs and car expenses.","cn":"最常见的经济支持类型包括手机套餐、食物、学费和汽车开支。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Parental financial support of early adults, said Ken Dychtwald, CEO of Age Wave, is \"the new normal\".","cn":"Age Wave 首席执行官 Ken Dychtwald 表示，父母对年轻成年人的经济支持是\"新常态\"。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"But 64% of the young adults surveyed said parents' financial support to children age 25 to 34 is \"a bad thing\", because it makes those kids dependent.","cn":"但 64% 接受调查的年轻成年人表示,父母对 25 至 34 岁子女的经济支持是\"坏事\",因为这会让这些孩子产生依赖性。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"By contrast, only 29% thought supporting men and women age 18 to 24 is bad; the remaining 71% think that assistance \"helps the adult children get ahead\".","cn":"相比之下,只有 29% 的人认为支持 18 至 24 岁的男性和女性是坏事;其余 71% 的人认为这种援助\"帮助成年子女取得进步\"。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Dychtwald believes the young women and men surveyed were saying that by 25, younger adults ought to be financially independent.","cn":"Dychtwald 认为,接受调查的年轻女性和男性表达的意思是,到 25 岁时,年轻成年人应该在经济上独立。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"In fact, the respondents said, financial independence defines adulthood.","cn":"事实上,受访者表示,经济独立定义了成年。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"\"Financial independence is something they were struggling with and challenged by.","cn":"\"经济独立是他们正在努力应对和面临挑战的事情。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"And it scared them a bit,\" Dychtwald said.","cn":"这让他们有点害怕,\" Dychtwald 说。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"One big reason they're struggling is attributed to college loans, of which the average amounts to $37,000.","cn":"他们面临困难的一个重要原因归结于大学贷款,平均金额为 37,000 美元。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Many of the parents have taken on college loans for the kids, too, sometimes at the expense of their own finances.","cn":"许多父母也为孩子承担了大学贷款,有时以牺牲自己的财务状况为代价。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"In the survey, 60% of early adults define financial success as being debt-free.","cn":"在调查中,60% 的年轻成年人将经济成功定义为无债务。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Whether that's likely, or even possible, anytime soon is anyone's guess.","cn":"这是否可能,甚至是否有可能在短期内实现,谁也说不准。"}]},{"id":"cet4-2024-06-2","level":"CET4","exam":"2024_06_2","year":2024,"month":6,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2024年6月 四级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2024年6月 CET-4 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet4-2024-06-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"A JetBlue Airlines flight from West Palm Beach to New York City was forced to turn around and land Sunday morning after the plane struck a bird.","cn":"JetBlue航空公司一架从西棕榈滩飞往纽约市的航班周日上午在飞机撞鸟后被迫掉头降落。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The flight from Palm Beach International Airport to LaGuardia Airport turned around just minutes after takeoff following the strike.","cn":"这架从棕榈滩国际机场飞往LaGuardia机场的航班在起飞仅几分钟后因撞击事件而掉头返航。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"No injuries were reported on the plane, and the flight took off once again 7.5 hours after the first attempt. \"It was like a split second of panic…that resulted in this nervous reaction on the plane,\" said passenger Brian Healy. \"There was total quiet, and then there was relief when the plane came to a stop.\" An email from JetBlue read, \"Our team is working to accommodate customers on later flights.\"","cn":"机上未报告有人员受伤,该航班在首次尝试起飞7.5小时后再次起飞。乘客Brian Healy说:\"那就像一瞬间的恐慌……导致机上出现紧张反应。机舱内一片寂静,当飞机停下来时大家才松了口气。\"JetBlue发送的一封电子邮件写道:\"我们的团队正在努力为乘客安排后续航班。\""},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"A deadly snake, which had finally been tracked down after escaping a zoo, has slipped away for the second time.","cn":"一条致命的毒蛇在从动物园逃脱后终于被追踪到,却第二次溜走了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The poisonous snake forced the closure of the attraction last week when staff noticed the disappearance.","cn":"上周当工作人员注意到这条毒蛇失踪时,它迫使该景点关闭。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"After six days of desperate searching, he was eventually found and placed in a supposedly secure area.","cn":"经过六天的拼命搜寻,它最终被找到并被安置在一个据称安全的区域。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"But it seems the animal is no fan of the zoo, because yet again he is out on the loose.","cn":"但这只动物似乎并不喜欢这家动物园,因为它再次逃脱了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The snake is a relative newcomer to the zoo but has already been frustrating its staff.","cn":"这条蛇是动物园相对较新的成员,但已经让工作人员感到沮丧。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The staff believe he squeezed himself out of a gap located around new energy-saving bulbs installed inside the snake house.","cn":"工作人员认为它是从蛇舍内安装的新型节能灯泡周围的缝隙中挤出去的。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"He was only found the first time around because staff brought in a special machine to trace him inside a wall opening.","cn":"它第一次被找到是因为工作人员带来了一台特殊的机器,在墙壁开口内追踪到了它。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"This kind of snake is one of the most deadly and poisonous in the wild, and they can range from 3 to 5 meters in length.","cn":"这种蛇是野外最致命、毒性最强的蛇类之一,体长可达3至5米。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Electric bikes have been the craze in downtown Jacksonville since they were first introduced earlier this month as a one-year pilot program.","cn":"自本月早些时候作为为期一年的试点项目首次引入以来,电动自行车在杰克逊维尔市中心引发了热潮。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"But they're leading to safety concerns, mainly at night when some riders don't follow the rules of the road.","cn":"但它们引发了安全担忧,主要是在夜间,一些骑行者不遵守交通规则。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"As the night goes on, groups of riders are often seen traveling in just about every direction in the streets and on pedestrian paths.","cn":"随着夜幕降临,经常可以看到成群的骑行者在街道和人行道上几乎朝着各个方向行驶。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"That is increasing the probability of dangerous accidents.","cn":"这增加了发生危险事故的可能性。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Electric bike riders have to follow all the same rules as you would if you were in an automobile.","cn":"电动自行车骑行者必须遵守与驾驶汽车时相同的所有规则。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"That means no running red lights or traveling in the opposite direction of traffic on one-way streets.","cn":"这意味着不能闯红灯,也不能在单行道上逆向行驶。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"City Council Member Anna Cumber was instrumental in introducing the electric bikes to Jacksonville as a way to bring new life into downtown. And she's aware of the concerns. Cumber said, \"People can have fun, but both drivers and riders are responsible for paying attention while on the road. And never assume the driver is going to stop or see you.\"","cn":"市议会成员Anna Cumber在将电动自行车引入杰克逊维尔以为市中心注入新活力方面发挥了重要作用。她也意识到了这些担忧。Cumber说:\"人们可以享受乐趣,但驾驶员和骑行者都有责任在路上保持注意力。永远不要假设驾驶员会停车或看到你。\""},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: What's the best way to teach children how to save and spend their money?","cn":"M: 教孩子如何存钱和花钱,最好的方法是什么?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: You should make money a regular topic of discussion.","cn":"W: 你应该把钱的话题作为日常讨论的内容。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's best to start young, so it's instinctive rather than a scary subject.","cn":"最好从小开始,这样就会成为本能反应,而不是一个可怕的话题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: In our family, we talk openly about things like the budget for holidays, how taxes reduce your income, and how to shop around for the best deals.","cn":"M: 在我们家,我们公开讨论像假期预算、税收如何减少你的收入,以及如何货比三家找到最优惠的价格这类事情。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Indeed.","cn":"W: 确实如此。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's also essential to make money real for children through practical examples.","cn":"通过实际例子让孩子对金钱有真实感受也很重要。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Working out how much we save using discount pizza coupons, for example, is much more relevant than abstract sums.","cn":"比如算出使用披萨折扣券能省多少钱,这比抽象的数字计算要实用得多。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: We also give our kids pocket money, and the amount they get is linked to chores, such as putting the bins out and emptying the dishwasher.","cn":"M: 我们还给孩子零花钱,金额多少跟家务挂钩,比如倒垃圾和清空洗碗机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: We do that too, and it's paid according to their age.","cn":"W: 我们也这样做,而且是按年龄支付。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Two pounds for each year so they can see some progression.","cn":"每岁两英镑,这样他们能看到一些进步。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Teaching them to save is important.","cn":"M: 教他们存钱很重要。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We opened a savings account when they were young.","cn":"我们在他们小时候就开了储蓄账户。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"After birthdays and Christmas, they would go to the branch and deposit their gift money.","cn":"生日和圣诞节过后,他们会去银行网点存入收到的礼金。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Oh, I hadn't considered doing that.","cn":"W: 哦,我还没考虑过这样做。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"In our house, we have transparent money boxes for them to put small change in, so they can see their savings grow.","cn":"在我们家,我们有透明的存钱罐让他们放零钱,这样他们能看到自己的储蓄增长。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: When the time is right, I'll start talking to our children about investing and show them how the money saved for their further education has grown.","cn":"M: 时机成熟时,我会开始跟孩子们谈投资,让他们看看为他们继续教育存的钱是如何增长的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I am always talking to my elder daughter about the importance of saving into a pension.","cn":"W: 我一直跟大女儿强调存养老金的重要性。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"She's just started a part-time job and was thinking of not contributing to her pension.","cn":"她刚开始做兼职,本来想着不缴纳养老金。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Luckily, I managed to persuade her otherwise.","cn":"幸好我说服了她。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Yes, it's such an important lesson to learn.","cn":"M: 是的,这是非常重要的一课。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Welcome to Books in Review.","cn":"W: 欢迎收看《书评》。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Our guest today is John Banks, the author of the best selling new book, Rewarding Success.","cn":"今天的嘉宾是畅销新书《奖励成功》的作者约翰·班克斯。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Glad to be here, Jane.","cn":"M: 很高兴来到这里,简。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Your book has sold 2 million copies, but before we discuss why it's getting so much attention, let's talk about your background.","cn":"W: 您的书已经售出200万册,但在我们讨论它为什么受到如此多关注之前,让我们先聊聊您的背景。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You're an economist and spent two decades teaching at universities?","cn":"您是一位经济学家,在大学教了二十年书?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I spent 25 years as a professor, actually.","cn":"M: 实际上我当了25年教授。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And then, for the last 10 years, I've worked as a political consultant, advising politicians at the national level about problems in our country.","cn":"然后,在过去10年里,我一直担任政治顾问,就我们国家的问题向国家层面的政治家们提供建议。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: You discuss three of those problems in the book, improving public education, reducing our nation's healthcare burden, and increasing personal savings.","cn":"W: 您在书中讨论了其中三个问题,改善公共教育、减轻我们国家的医疗负担以及增加个人储蓄。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But your ideas about education are the most controversial.","cn":"但您关于教育的观点是最具争议的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Absolutely.","cn":"M: 没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"A lot of people think I'm trying to punish students who aren't doing well, when actually my goal is to give all students more incentive to succeed.","cn":"很多人认为我是在惩罚那些表现不好的学生,而实际上我的目标是给所有学生更多成功的动力。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I'm not sure I agree with you. Your proposal to pay cash rewards to students who get good grades is a particular problem. What about students who don't get good grades? It seems like you're blaming them for not succeeding, when poor performance in school isn't a child's fault.","cn":"W: 我不确定我是否同意您的观点。您提议向成绩好的学生支付现金奖励,这是个特别的问题。那成绩不好的学生怎么办?看起来您是在责怪他们不成功,而在学校表现不佳并不是孩子的错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: But my proposal is not just to reward students with good grades, but also students who show improvements.","cn":"M: 但我的提议不仅是奖励成绩好的学生,也奖励那些有进步的学生。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Okay, another criticism of the plan is the cash rewards themselves.","cn":"W: 好吧,这个计划的另一个批评是现金奖励本身。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Where will the money come from?","cn":"钱从哪里来?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: If students do better, we'll spend less on schooling.","cn":"M: 如果学生们表现更好,我们在教育上的花费就会减少。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So, in the end, the rewards will pay for themselves.","cn":"所以,最终这些奖励会自己收回成本。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: What about now? How will we fund the rewards in the meantime?","cn":"W: 那现在呢?在此期间我们如何资助这些奖励?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, by increasing taxes or moving money from other areas of the budget into education.","cn":"M: 嗯,通过增加税收或者从预算的其他领域把钱转移到教育上。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"I met three different people today, and each time, when I asked, \"How are you?\" The reply was exactly the same. \"I'm busy\". Honestly, I hear the same answer from the vast majority of people I meet. So I started to think: \"Guess what? Everybody's busy!\" I'm busy, you're busy, everybody's busy. So you being busy doesn't make me sympathetic at all. Because \"busy\" is the state of the world.","cn":"我今天遇到了三个不同的人,每次当我问\"你好吗?\"时,得到的回答都一模一样。\"我很忙\"。老实说,我遇到的绝大多数人都给我同样的答案。所以我开始思考:\"你猜怎么着?每个人都很忙!\"我很忙,你很忙,每个人都很忙。所以你忙根本不会让我感到同情。因为\"忙\"就是这个世界的常态。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"So I'm launching a campaign to stop people complaining about being \"busy.\" It may sound harsh, but the truth is, nobody cares. In a busy world, \"being busy\" doesn't stand out, nor does it mean productive, creative, accomplished, or professional.","cn":"所以我正在发起一项运动,呼吁人们停止抱怨自己\"很忙\"。这听起来可能有点刺耳,但事实是,没有人在乎。在一个忙碌的世界里,\"忙碌\"并不突出,也不意味着高效、有创造力、有成就或专业。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Steve Maraboli once said, \"When someone tells you they are too 'busy', it's not a reflection of their schedule; it's a reflection of YOUR spot on their schedule.\" Donna Lynn Hope has also remarked, \"Busy doesn't mean better. I've never envied a busy person—the one who likes to point out their busy lives to others.\"","cn":"Steve Maraboli曾经说过:\"当有人告诉你他们太'忙'时,这不是反映他们的日程安排;而是反映了你在他们日程安排中的位置。\"Donna Lynn Hope也评论道:\"忙碌并不意味着更好。我从不羡慕忙碌的人——那种喜欢向别人强调自己生活有多忙的人。\""},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The reality is, nobody is too busy—it's just about priorities.","cn":"现实是,没有人真的太忙——这只是关乎优先级的问题。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"So the next time someone asks you how you are, maybe respond differently.","cn":"所以下次有人问你过得怎么样时,也许可以换一种回答方式。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"In my experience, the \"I'm busy\" response is really covering up the fact that they're not actually accomplishing their real purpose.","cn":"根据我的经验,\"我很忙\"这个回答实际上是在掩盖他们并没有真正完成自己真正目标的事实。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"And \"being busy\" is the lie they tell themselves about why they can't achieve it.","cn":"而\"忙碌\"是他们对自己无法实现目标所撒的谎。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"More and more people are taking up extreme sports, like snowboarding, skateboarding, mountain biking, and many more.","cn":"越来越多的人开始从事极限运动,如滑雪板、滑板、山地自行车等等。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Why are these sports becoming so popular?","cn":"为什么这些运动变得如此流行?"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"One thing that extreme sports do better than perhaps anything else is to help you stop being afraid.","cn":"极限运动比其他任何事物都更能帮助你克服恐惧。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It may sound strange to say that their main function is to reduce fear.","cn":"说它们的主要功能是减少恐惧可能听起来很奇怪。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But after a time, your fear response to other things in life will be dramatically reduced.","cn":"但一段时间后,你对生活中其他事物的恐惧反应将会大幅减少。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"After all, if you can jump out of a plane or off a bridge, then you can face anything else easily.","cn":"毕竟,如果你能从飞机上或桥上跳下来,那么你就能轻松面对其他任何事情。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"When doing extreme sports, you have to become more focused.","cn":"在进行极限运动时,你必须变得更加专注。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"You'll be pushed to your limits, and if you aren't focused you'll make dangerous mistakes.","cn":"你会被推向极限,如果不够专注就会犯下危险的错误。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Learning to be this focused when enjoying extreme sports will help you to be focused at work, keeping you more productive and ultimately more successful.","cn":"在享受极限运动时学会如此专注将帮助你在工作中保持专注,使你更高效,最终更成功。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It's great to stay fit and healthy, but standard exercise routines and sports only work the same muscles repeatedly. With extreme sports, you'll be working entirely different muscles, and that means you get an all-over workout. Extreme sports also burn a lot more calories than other sports. Skateboarding, for example, can burn as many as 500 calories per hour. Basketball burns around 300 in the same time.","cn":"保持健康很重要,但标准的锻炼程序和运动只会反复锻炼相同的肌肉。通过极限运动,你会锻炼到完全不同的肌肉,这意味着你能得到全身锻炼。极限运动消耗的卡路里也比其他运动多得多。例如,滑板每小时可以消耗多达500卡路里,而篮球在同样时间内消耗约300卡路里。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"When you find that you can overcome the physical or mental challenges involved in extreme sports, you'll feel superhuman and your self-confidence will be at an all-time high.","cn":"当你发现自己能够克服极限运动中的身体或心理挑战时,你会感觉自己无所不能,自信心将达到前所未有的高度。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Most of us have been in teams or organizations where we've had conflict with the people that we're working with around the ideas or decisions that we're discussing.","cn":"我们大多数人都曾身处这样的团队或组织：在讨论想法或决策时，与合作者产生冲突。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Conflict is natural.","cn":"冲突是自然的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"We all bring different life and work experiences to the table.","cn":"我们每个人都带来不同的生活和工作经验。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"We all have different personality preferences and tendencies.","cn":"我们都有不同的性格偏好和倾向。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"We're not all going to have the same ideas on how to approach policies, programs or problems.","cn":"我们不可能在如何处理政策、项目或问题上都有相同的想法。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"But too often we get caught in this place where conflict is perceived to be negative—something we want to avoid so that we can maintain the harmony of our workplace.","cn":"但我们经常陷入这样一种境地：冲突被视为负面的——我们想要避免的东西，以便维持工作场所的和谐。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This could be because some people want to avoid conflict at all costs, after all they still have to work together.","cn":"这可能是因为有些人想不惜一切代价避免冲突,毕竟他们还要继续共事。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"But this kind of artificial harmony isn't the answer.","cn":"但这种人为的和谐并不是答案。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Productive conflict is a vital part of teams and organizations that want to push forward and do more.","cn":"建设性冲突是想要向前推进并做得更多的团队和组织的重要组成部分。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Without conflict, we're often stuck in this artificial harmony where people don't express potentially innovative ideas for fear that they may start conflict with others.","cn":"没有冲突,我们往往会陷入这种人为的和谐,人们不敢表达可能具有创新性的想法,因为担心可能会与他人产生冲突。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"But if you're in a place where you have a basis of trust, conflict can be extremely productive.","cn":"但如果你所在的地方有信任的基础,冲突可以极具建设性。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"It can lead to increased innovation and greater trust on teams.","cn":"它可以带来更多创新和团队间更大的信任。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"It may be an uncomfortable process, but good leaders and healthy teams recognize that productive and healthy conflict is an important part of how they function.","cn":"这可能是一个令人不适的过程,但优秀的领导者和健康的团队认识到,建设性和健康的冲突是他们运作方式的重要组成部分。"}]},{"id":"cet4-2024-12-1","level":"CET4","exam":"2024_12_1","year":2024,"month":12,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2024年12月 四级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2024年12月 CET-4 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet4-2024-12-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The City of Fayetteville is making a special effort to recognize its bus drivers ahead of the newly proclaimed Transit Driver Appreciation Day happening Saturday.","cn":"Fayetteville市正在特别努力表彰其公交车司机，以迎接新设立的公交司机感谢日，该日定于周六举行。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"As part of the event, the city is celebrating its longest-serving driver on the force.","cn":"作为活动的一部分,该市正在庆祝其服务时间最长的在职司机。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"That driver is Sherry Christian.","cn":"这位司机是Sherry Christian。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Christian has been a driver for 25 years.","cn":"Christian已经担任司机25年。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The Fayetteville native believes driving a school bus allows her to give back to her community.","cn":"这位Fayetteville本地人认为驾驶校车让她能够回馈社区。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"She says that the best part of the job is watching the children who ride her bus grow up.","cn":"她说这份工作最好的部分是看着乘坐她的校车的孩子们长大。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Transit Driver Appreciation Day has been celebrated across the country as far back as 2009.","cn":"公交司机感谢日早在2009年就在全国范围内庆祝。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"However, this week, the City of Fayetteville issued a proclamation for the day to take place March 18th.","cn":"然而,本周Fayetteville市发布公告将这一日期定为3月18日。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Officials said they want bus drivers to know how important they are to Fayetteville, serving almost 1.6 million riders a year.","cn":"官员们表示,他们希望公交车司机知道他们对Fayetteville有多么重要,每年为近160万名乘客提供服务。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The Wilton School Board has proposed a 5.99% spending increase.","cn":"Wilton学区委员会提议增加5.99%的支出。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"If approved, it would be the largest jump in at least eight budget cycles.","cn":"如果获得批准,这将是至少八个预算周期中最大的增幅。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The 5.99% request more than doubles the highest previous year-over-year increase in the last eight years, which was 2.99% for the 2021-2022 school year.","cn":"5.99%的增幅请求是过去八年中最高年度增幅的两倍多,而此前最高增幅是2021-2022学年的2.99%。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The biggest driver of the $91.8 million proposed budget remains teacher salaries.","cn":"这份9180万美元预算提案的最大驱动因素仍然是教师工资。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"These account for 64% of the total request at $59 million.","cn":"教师工资占总请求金额的64%,为5900万美元。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The $59 million is up from the $56.7 million budgeted for the current school year.","cn":"5900万美元高于本学年预算的5670万美元。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"There are some factors that could affect the budget moving forward.","cn":"有一些因素可能会影响未来的预算。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"One of those is total enrollment.","cn":"其中之一是总入学人数。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The district will have a total enrollment of 3,742 students.","cn":"该学区将有3742名学生入学。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Almost all of these students will be in kindergarten through high school, but 66 will be in prekindergarten and other programs.","cn":"几乎所有这些学生都将在幼儿园到高中阶段就读,但有66名学生将在学前班和其他项目中。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"This represents 47 fewer students than the current year.","cn":"这比本学年减少了47名学生。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Fewer students mean less federal and state funding.","cn":"学生人数减少意味着联邦和州拨款减少。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"A rare thundersnow event has taken place in Scotland.","cn":"苏格兰发生了一次罕见的雷雪事件。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"And alarmed locals contacted police, thinking they had heard bombs going off.","cn":"惊慌失措的当地居民联系了警方,以为他们听到了炸弹爆炸的声音。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The phenomenon happens when thunder and lightning mix with a heavy snowstorm—sometimes causing loud claps that can be confused with explosions.","cn":"这种现象发生在雷电与暴雪混合时,有时会产生巨大的爆裂声,容易被误认为是爆炸。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"One person described it as a loud boom, similar to a plane crash.","cn":"一个人将其描述为一声巨响,类似于飞机坠毁。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Another person was woken up in the middle of the night by what he thought was early construction work starting.","cn":"另一个人在半夜被他以为是早期施工开始的声音吵醒。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The noise was powerful enough to shake buildings and set off car alarms.","cn":"这种噪音强大到足以震动建筑物并触发汽车警报器。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The police were flooded with many calls from the public.","cn":"警方接到了大量公众来电。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"And they sent out a message asking people to remain calm.","cn":"他们发出信息要求人们保持冷静。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The police assured everyone that it was just thunder and lightning rather than some military exercise.","cn":"警方向所有人保证这只是雷电,而不是什么军事演习。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The weather was the coldest it had been for the season, so people were warned to be careful when traveling outside.","cn":"天气是本季最冷的,因此人们被警告在外出时要小心。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"In particular, dangerous conditions such as icy roads or wet ground could cause difficulty for drivers.","cn":"特别是结冰的道路或湿滑的地面等危险状况可能会给司机造成困难。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The rail service also announced potential disruptions to trains due to the deep snow.","cn":"铁路部门也宣布由于积雪深厚,列车可能会受到干扰。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Some roads were also closed because of the severe weather.","cn":"一些道路也因恶劣天气而关闭。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I'm going to the city centre to buy a new phone today.","cn":"M: 我今天要去市中心买一部新手机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Didn't you buy a new phone just two months ago?","cn":"W: 你不是两个月前才买了一部新手机吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: It was three months ago, and I already know what you're going to say.","cn":"M: 是三个月前,而且我已经知道你要说什么了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"You're thinking I shouldn't replace my phone this soon.","cn":"你觉得我不该这么快就换手机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: No, actually, I was wondering how you could possibly afford a new phone.","cn":"W: 不,其实我是在想你怎么可能负担得起一部新手机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But now that you mention it, I do think getting another phone so soon is wasteful, regardless of the cost.","cn":"但既然你提到了,我确实认为这么快又买一部手机很浪费,不管多少钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Maybe you're right, but the thing is, everyone at the office has a nice, expensive phone, and I'm a little embarrassed by mine.","cn":"M: 也许你说得对,但问题是,办公室里每个人都有一部很好很贵的手机,我对我的手机有点难为情。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I just got a credit card, so I thought I might as well buy a new phone.","cn":"我刚办了一张信用卡,所以我想不如买部新手机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I don't think buying a phone on credit is a good idea.","cn":"W: 我觉得用信用卡买手机不是个好主意。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Look, you've only been working for five months now.","cn":"你看,你才工作了五个月。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"People understand that you are a recent graduate, and I doubt anyone cares about your phone other than yourself.","cn":"大家都理解你是刚毕业的,我觉得除了你自己,没人在意你的手机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Maybe you're right, but the credit card has a very good special offer, where I don't pay any interest for six months.","cn":"M: 也许你说得对,但这张信用卡有一个很好的特别优惠,六个月内不用付利息。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I'll be able to pay for the phone well before that period is over.","cn":"在那之前我肯定能把手机款付清。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I still think it's a bad idea to use a credit card for something you don't need.","cn":"W: 我还是觉得用信用卡买你不需要的东西是个坏主意。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"One of my colleagues bought a lot of things on credit during her first year of work, and it became a bad habit, and she accumulated a lot of debt.","cn":"我有个同事在工作第一年用信用卡买了很多东西,这变成了一个坏习惯,她积累了很多债务。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Well, I can see how that might happen to someone, and I'm sure she regrets it, but I know it won't happen to me.","cn":"M: 嗯,我能理解这种事可能发生在某些人身上,我相信她很后悔,但我知道这不会发生在我身上。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Welcome to The Morning Show.","cn":"W: 欢迎来到《早间秀》。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Our guest today is a popular blog writer and a major figure in the tiny home community.","cn":"我们今天的嘉宾是一位人气博主,也是迷你住宅社区的重要人物。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Welcome, Bob Jones.","cn":"欢迎你,Bob Jones。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Hi, Mary.","cn":"M: 你好,Mary。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Hi, Bob.","cn":"W: 你好,Bob。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You're an advocate of the tiny home movement.","cn":"你是迷你住宅运动的倡导者。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"A lot of people don't know about this movement.","cn":"很多人不了解这个运动。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Can you tell our audience what it's about?","cn":"你能给我们的观众介绍一下它是怎么回事吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, it's mainly about increasing home ownership and protecting the environment.","cn":"M: 嗯,它主要是关于提高住房拥有率和保护环境。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Of course, those are great goals.","cn":"W: 当然,这些都是很好的目标。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But I've seen your blog, and you write about houses that are as small as 20 square meters.","cn":"但我看过你的博客,你写的房子小到只有20平方米。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"That's not a realistic size for families.","cn":"这对家庭来说不是一个现实的面积。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I do talk about very small homes, but there's no set definition of a tiny home.","cn":"M: 我确实谈论过非常小的房子,但迷你住宅没有固定的定义。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And other people include homes that are much larger, say, 60 square meters.","cn":"其他人也包括大得多的房子,比如说60平方米。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And you'd be surprised many families of four are happy living in houses that are under 30 square meters.","cn":"你会惊讶地发现,许多四口之家很乐意住在不到30平方米的房子里。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: But I think most of us want spacious homes.","cn":"W: 但我认为我们大多数人都想要宽敞的房子。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"The average new house in this area is 150 square meters.","cn":"这个地区新房的平均面积是150平方米。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And that's what people dream of owning.","cn":"这就是人们梦想拥有的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Yes, but I think that dream needs to change, considering the cost of housing.","cn":"M: 是的,但考虑到住房成本,我认为这个梦想需要改变。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Housing costs are high, but do people really save that much by having a smaller home?","cn":"W: 住房成本很高,但人们通过拥有更小的房子真的能省那么多钱吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Absolutely.","cn":"M: 当然。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Many people who can only afford to rent a large home are able to buy a tiny home.","cn":"许多只能租得起大房子的人能够买得起迷你住宅。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"In this city, the average home costs $200,000, and a tiny home costs just $50,000.","cn":"在这个城市,普通住宅的平均价格是20万美元,而迷你住宅只需5万美元。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Those are huge savings.","cn":"W: 这可是巨大的节省。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: So, tiny homes might not be for everyone, but they're a good option for many.","cn":"M: 所以,迷你住宅可能不适合所有人,但对许多人来说是个不错的选择。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: You mentioned the environment earlier.","cn":"W: 你之前提到了环境。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"How does this benefit the planet?","cn":"这如何造福地球呢?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, if people have smaller homes, they use less land and fewer resources to build them.","cn":"M: 嗯,如果人们住更小的房子,他们就会使用更少的土地和更少的资源来建造它们。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Kids need time every day to run, jump, stretch and play.","cn":"孩子们每天都需要时间来跑步、跳跃、伸展和玩耍。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"These experiences have been shown to build children's confidence and pleasure in physical activities, develop their motor skills, and even improve emotional well-being.","cn":"这些经历已被证明能够建立儿童对体育活动的信心和乐趣,发展他们的运动技能,甚至改善情绪健康。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"To begin with, children seem to have a natural desire to overcome challenges and take risks.","cn":"首先,儿童似乎天生就有克服挑战和冒险的欲望。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Taking healthy risks through physical movement builds children's confidence and ability to solve problems and persist through frustration.","cn":"通过身体运动进行健康的冒险可以建立儿童的信心和解决问题的能力,并在挫折中坚持下去。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Secondly, movement activities build children's big body skills such as coordination and balance, as well as the fine motor skills they need for tasks like writing, tying their shoes, or throwing and catching a ball.","cn":"其次,运动活动可以培养儿童的大肌肉运动技能,如协调性和平衡性,以及他们完成写字、系鞋带或投掷接球等任务所需的精细运动技能。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Thirdly, according to the American Psychological Association, regular physical activity (and especially outdoor activity) reduces children's stress and depression, and improves their ability to focus and learn.","cn":"第三,根据美国心理学会的研究,定期的体育活动(尤其是户外活动)可以减轻儿童的压力和抑郁,并提高他们的专注力和学习能力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Regular exercise can significantly improve self-regulation and decrease disciplinary consequences for negative behavior.","cn":"定期锻炼可以显著改善自我调节能力,并减少因不良行为而受到的纪律处分。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Physical activity provides a positive outlet for frustration, anxiety, or anger and can become a healthy coping skill throughout life.","cn":"体育活动为挫折、焦虑或愤怒提供了一个积极的出口,并可以成为贯穿一生的健康应对技能。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Finally, we know that physical activity is important for our physical and mental health, and cultivating the habit of physical activity starts early.","cn":"最后,我们知道体育活动对我们的身心健康很重要,而培养体育活动的习惯要从小开始。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Children are more likely to develop a lifelong love of physical activity from frequent positive early experiences.","cn":"儿童更有可能从频繁的积极早期经历中培养出对体育活动的终身热爱。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Not every child enjoys competitive sports or playing with balls and that's OK.","cn":"并非每个孩子都喜欢竞技体育或玩球类运动,这没关系。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"There are plenty of other options such as imaginative play, non-competitive games, and gardening or nature experiences.","cn":"还有很多其他选择,如想象性游戏、非竞争性游戏以及园艺或自然体验。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"A new study finds that job seekers are even willing to explore jobs with lower salaries when companies are more diverse.","cn":"一项新研究发现，当公司更具多样性时，求职者甚至愿意探索薪资较低的工作。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It finds that sharing information about diversity makes job postings more attractive to job seekers, even when pay is lower.","cn":"研究发现，分享关于多样性的信息使得招聘信息对求职者更具吸引力，即使薪酬较低。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"To conduct the study, the team partnered with an online job listings platform which emails postings relevant to individuals and their job search criteria.","cn":"为了进行这项研究，研究团队与一个在线招聘信息平台合作，该平台会向个人发送与其求职标准相关的职位信息邮件。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For the course of the 11-week study, the platform emailed job listings to some 180,000 users placed in one of two conditions.","cn":"在为期11周的研究过程中，该平台向约18万名用户发送招聘信息邮件，这些用户被分为两种情况之一。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In the baseline condition, participants saw emails in the normal format, with no information on diversity; in the diversity condition, participants saw a diversity score for each listing: information about the race, gender, education, and language skills of a company's workforce compared to others in the same sector and location.","cn":"在基线情况下，参与者看到的是正常格式的邮件,没有关于多样性的信息;在多样性情况下,参与者看到每个招聘信息的多样性评分:关于公司员工的种族、性别、教育程度和语言技能与同一行业和地区其他公司相比的信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Information was then gathered on whether the email was opened, and which job listings were clicked on by each user.","cn":"然后收集关于邮件是否被打开以及每个用户点击了哪些招聘信息的数据。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Participants in the diversity condition tended to click on job listings from companies with slightly higher diversity scores than those in the baseline condition: that is, participants seemed to be paying attention to information about diversity, and using this when deciding whether to click on the listing.","cn":"多样性情况下的参与者倾向于点击多样性评分略高于基线情况下公司的招聘信息:也就是说，参与者似乎关注关于多样性的信息，并在决定是否点击该招聘信息时使用这些信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"And the team also found that participants were willing to look at listings with lower salaries if they came from companies with a higher diversity score.","cn":"研究团队还发现，如果招聘信息来自多样性评分较高的公司，参与者愿意查看薪资较低的招聘信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"A new study from Oregon State University found that dogs tend to match their behavior with the children in their family.","cn":"俄勒冈州立大学的一项新研究发现，狗往往会使自己的行为与家庭中的儿童相匹配。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The findings are important because there is a growing body of evidence that dogs can help children in many ways.","cn":"这些发现很重要，因为越来越多的证据表明狗可以在许多方面帮助儿童。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"These include helping with social development, increasing physical activity, managing anxiety or serving as a source of attachment in the face of changing family structures.","cn":"这些方面包括帮助社交发展、增加身体活动、管理焦虑或在家庭结构变化时充当依恋来源。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Yet, very little research has focused on how dogs perceive and socially engage with children. \"The great news is that this study suggests dogs are paying a lot of attention to the kids that they live with,\" said Monique Udell, the lead author of the study. \"One interesting thing we have observed is that dogs are matching children's behavior, but less frequently than what we have seen between dogs and adults. This suggests that while dogs may view children as social companions, there are also some differences that we need to understand better.\"","cn":"然而，很少有研究关注狗如何感知儿童并与儿童进行社交互动。该研究的主要作者Monique Udell说：\"好消息是，这项研究表明狗非常关注与它们一起生活的孩子。我们观察到的一个有趣现象是，狗会匹配儿童的行为，但频率低于我们在狗和成人之间观察到的情况。这表明虽然狗可能将儿童视为社交伙伴，但也存在一些我们需要更好理解的差异。\""},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"While research has found dogs can have a lot of positive impacts on a child's life, there are also risks associated with the dog-child relationship. For example, other studies have found dogs are more likely to bite children versus adults. \"We still have a lot to learn about the dog-child relationship,\" Udell said. \"But research does show that kids are very capable of training dogs.\"","cn":"虽然研究发现狗可以对儿童的生活产生许多积极影响，但狗与儿童的关系也存在风险。例如，其他研究发现狗咬儿童的可能性高于咬成人。Udell说：\"关于狗与儿童的关系，我们还有很多需要了解的。但研究确实表明，孩子们非常有能力训练狗。\""}]},{"id":"cet4-2024-12-2","level":"CET4","exam":"2024_12_2","year":2024,"month":12,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2024年12月 四级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2024年12月 CET-4 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet4-2024-12-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"U.S. families are looking to the winter with fear as energy costs soar.","cn":"随着能源成本飙升,美国家庭正怀着恐惧展望这个冬天。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"A number of factors are creating a bad situation: Global energy consumption is up, but supplies have been reduced.","cn":"多种因素正在造成糟糕的局面:全球能源消费增加,但供应却减少了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The Energy Department projects heating bills will jump 28% this winter for those who rely on natural gas.","cn":"能源部预测,依赖天然气供暖的家庭今年冬天的取暖费用将跃升28%。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Natural gas is used by nearly half of U.S. households for heat.","cn":"近一半的美国家庭使用天然气供暖。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Heating oil is projected to be 27% higher and electricity 10% higher.","cn":"取暖用油预计将上涨27%,电费将上涨10%。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"That comes against inflation rates that accelerated last month with consumer prices growing 6.6%.","cn":"这是在通胀率加速的背景下发生的,上个月消费者价格上涨了6.6%。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"That's the fastest pace in four decades.","cn":"这是四十年来最快的增速。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The pain will be especially acute in parts of the country that heavily rely on heating oil to keep homes warm.","cn":"在严重依赖取暖用油保持家庭温暖的地区,这种痛苦将尤为剧烈。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"It's projected to cost more than $2,300 to heat a typical home with heating oil this winter.","cn":"预计今年冬天用取暖用油为一个典型家庭供暖将花费超过2300美元。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Last month, the federal government added $1 billion in funding to Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program, bringing the total to $4.8 billion.","cn":"上个月,联邦政府向低收入家庭能源援助计划增加了10亿美元资金,使总额达到48亿美元。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"But that represents a reduction from last year's energy assistance package of over $8 billion.","cn":"但这比去年超过80亿美元的能源援助计划有所减少。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Many Americans think they make healthy food choices, but they may be viewing their diet too optimistically.","cn":"许多美国人认为自己做出了健康的食物选择，但他们可能对自己的饮食过于乐观了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"That's the main finding of a new study by researchers at the U.S. Department of Agriculture in Stoneville, Mississippi.","cn":"这是美国农业部位于密西西比州Stoneville的研究人员一项新研究的主要发现。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The study aimed to identify disconnects between how healthily Americans think they eat and how they actually do.","cn":"该研究旨在找出美国人认为自己吃得有多健康与实际情况之间的差距。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"For the study, the researchers asked participants to rate their diet as excellent, very good, good, fair or poor.","cn":"在研究中，研究人员要求参与者将自己的饮食评为优秀、非常好、好、一般或差。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Folks also completed 24-hour food questionnaires.","cn":"参与者还完成了24小时食物问卷。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Then, the researchers compared answers to see how well responses to the two exercises matched up.","cn":"然后，研究人员比较了答案，看两项调查的回答匹配程度如何。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Of more than 9,700 people, roughly 85 percent were off base when asked to rate the quality of their diet, and almost all overestimated how healthy it was.","cn":"在9700多人中，大约85%的人在被要求评价自己的饮食质量时偏离了实际情况，而且几乎所有人都高估了饮食的健康程度。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Those who rated their diet as poor tended to be far more accurate.","cn":"那些将自己的饮食评为差的人往往准确得多。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Their rating matched that of the researchers more than nine times out of ten.","cn":"他们的评价在十次中有九次以上与研究人员的评价相符。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"It was a heartwarming moment that dozens of Indian rescuers rallied together to use a crane in order to save an elephant trapped at the bottom of a 20-foot well.","cn":"这是一个温馨的时刻，数十名印度救援人员齐心协力使用起重机营救一头困在20英尺深井底的大象。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The massive rescue effort took place last week close to an army camp.","cn":"这次大规模救援行动上周在一个军营附近进行。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The elephant wandered out of the jungle and fell into the well.","cn":"这头大象从丛林中走出来后掉进了井里。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The army officers heard a noise coming from the well and realized an elephant was trapped deep inside.","cn":"军官们听到井里传来声音，发现有一头大象被困在深处。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The officers then threw in some food for the creature and called the local forest department for help.","cn":"随后军官们向井里投放了一些食物，并向当地林业部门求助。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Video of the rescue operation shows how the team used a crane to lift up the huge animal out of the well and onto the back of a truck.","cn":"救援行动的视频显示，救援队如何使用起重机将这头巨大的动物从井里吊起并放到卡车后部。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"It was then taken to an examining room for evaluation of any injuries.","cn":"随后大象被送往检查室评估是否有任何伤情。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The elephant was kept under close supervision for a few days before it was successfully released back into the wild.","cn":"这头大象在密切监护下待了几天后被成功放归野外。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I need to stop at the bank to withdraw some cash.","cn":"M: 我得去银行取点现金。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Why not just pay with your phone?","cn":"W: 为什么不直接用手机支付呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Well, actually, I've stopped using online payments for the past three months now.","cn":"M: 嗯，实际上，我已经三个月没用线上支付了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Stopped paying online?","cn":"W: 不用线上支付了？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Oh, you must be worried that online payments aren't secure.","cn":"哦，你一定是担心线上支付不安全吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: No, they are safe.","cn":"M: 不，它们是安全的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But paying online is too convenient and I spent too much money on things I didn't need.","cn":"但线上支付太方便了，我在不需要的东西上花了太多钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Oh, impulse purchases can be an issue for me, too.","cn":"W: 哦，冲动消费对我来说也是个问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I've definitely bought clothes and shoes I didn't need because they were on sale, and paying with my phone was so easy.","cn":"我确实买过不需要的衣服和鞋子，因为它们在打折，而且用手机支付太容易了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But I've found that if I review my spending every night, that keeps me from spending too much.","cn":"但我发现如果每晚检查一下我的开支，就能控制住不花太多钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I tried that strategy, but it just didn't work, because I'd be busy studying all day.","cn":"M: 我试过那个办法，但没用，因为我一整天都在忙着学习。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Then, when I was tired and hungry, I'd use my phone to order food, like burgers and other junk, instead of going to the canteen, where I could get a healthier meal for half the price.","cn":"然后，当我又累又饿的时候，我就会用手机点外卖，比如汉堡和其他垃圾食品，而不是去食堂，在那里我可以花一半的价钱吃到更健康的饭菜。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Well, what do you do now then?","cn":"W: 那你现在怎么办呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It seems like you'd have the same problems with cash.","cn":"感觉你用现金也会有同样的问题啊。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I go to the bank once a week, and the rest of the time I keep my bank card at home, so I can't get more cash out.","cn":"M: 我每周去一次银行，其余时间把银行卡放在家里，这样我就取不到更多现金了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And I also have a notebook where I record my expenses.","cn":"而且我还有个笔记本记录我的开支。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: But what prevents you from just going to the bank and getting more money, if you want to buy something?","cn":"W: 但如果你想买东西，有什么能阻止你直接去银行取更多钱呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: The first month I did withdraw extra cash twice, but I felt guilty about it.","cn":"M: 第一个月我确实又取了两次额外的现金，但我为此感到内疚。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And after that I refused to spend more than what I had budgeted, and by now it's just a habit.","cn":"之后我就拒绝花超出预算的钱，到现在这已经成了习惯。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Please hear me out. I don't want our son to spend his afternoons doing something he hates, even if it might prepare him for the future. What about getting him to join a sport, like soccer? From all the running and training, he could become quite athletic. Not to mention the great physical benefits from exercising outside every day.","cn":"M: 请听我说完。我不想让我们的儿子把下午时间花在他讨厌的事情上,即使这可能为他的未来做准备。让他参加一项运动怎么样,比如足球?通过所有的跑步和训练,他可以变得很健壮。更不用说每天在户外锻炼带来的巨大身体益处了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Um, I don't think he should be doing something so challenging with all his breathing issues. What about playing an indoor sport, like badminton? The environment is easier to control, and he can still get a good workout, in addition to improving his hand-eye coordination. Besides, I could teach him some of the basics from my time as a badminton player.","cn":"W: 嗯,我觉得他不应该做这么有挑战性的事情,他有那么多呼吸问题。室内运动怎么样,比如羽毛球?环境更容易控制,他仍然可以得到很好的锻炼,还能提高手眼协调能力。而且,我可以教他一些基础知识,我以前是打羽毛球的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Um, I'm thinking team sports should be the way to go.","cn":"M: 嗯,我觉得应该选团队运动。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"There's nothing like playing as part of a unit to accomplish a goal like winning a game or even a championship.","cn":"没有什么比作为团队的一员去完成一个目标更好的了,比如赢得一场比赛甚至一个冠军。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"He could try basketball since many of the courts are indoors now and it's a sport that could help him understand team spirit while cooperating with others.","cn":"他可以试试篮球,因为现在很多球场都在室内,这项运动可以帮助他在与他人合作的同时理解团队精神。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Maybe he could even join the school basketball team when he's ready.","cn":"也许等他准备好了,他甚至可以加入学校篮球队。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Oh, oh, what about volleyball? It's a team sport and they often have mixed-gender teams so he could socialize with both girls and boys. It's not as popular as some sports, which means he has better odds of possibly getting an athletic scholarship in the future. I also believe you were a beach volleyball athlete yourself not so long ago.","cn":"W: 哦,哦,排球怎么样?这是一项团队运动,他们经常有男女混合队,所以他可以和女孩和男孩都社交。它不像有些运动那么受欢迎,这意味着他将来获得体育奖学金的机会更大。我还记得你不久前自己就是沙滩排球运动员。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: As I've said many times before, beach volleyball and indoor volleyball are completely different.","cn":"M: 正如我之前说过很多次的,沙滩排球和室内排球是完全不同的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Lift-off is usually the most environmentally harmful stage of any space mission, with vast quantities of fuel burnt up in a matter of minutes.","cn":"发射通常是任何太空任务中对环境危害最大的阶段,在短短几分钟内燃烧掉大量燃料。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"For instance, SpaceX's Falcon 9 gets through 112 tonnes of refined fuel, emitting about 336 tonnes of CO₂.","cn":"例如,SpaceX的猎鹰9号消耗112吨精炼燃料,排放约336吨二氧化碳。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"This is the equivalent produced by your average car driving almost 70 times around the world.","cn":"这相当于普通汽车绕地球行驶近70圈所产生的排放量。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"As well as greenhouse gases, rocket engines emit particles that destroy ozone.","cn":"除了温室气体,火箭发动机还排放破坏臭氧的颗粒物。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"These issues are growing more pressing with the emergence of commercial spaceflight.","cn":"随着商业太空飞行的兴起,这些问题变得越来越紧迫。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"There were 114 space launches in 2020, but there may be up to 1,000 per year in future.","cn":"2020年有114次太空发射,但未来每年可能多达1000次。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Sustainable fuels are the top priority to enable greener space travel.","cn":"可持续燃料是实现更环保太空旅行的首要任务。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Current spacecraft use a variety of fuels, but most are based on fossil fuels.","cn":"目前的航天器使用多种燃料,但大多数基于化石燃料。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"One potentially greener option is liquid hydrogen and oxygen.","cn":"一种潜在的更环保选择是液氢和液氧。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Hydrogen can be obtained sustainably by using solar power to break water down into oxygen and hydrogen.","cn":"氢可以通过利用太阳能将水分解成氧和氢来可持续地获得。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Reusable rockets can cut down on some of the waste associated with spaceflight.","cn":"可重复使用的火箭可以减少与太空飞行相关的一些浪费。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Traditionally, boosters, fuel tanks and other components are treated as expendable.","cn":"传统上,助推器、燃料箱和其他部件被视为一次性消耗品。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But guiding them back to Earth in a controlled manner opens new possibilities — most components from the Falcon 9 can be reused up to 100 times.","cn":"但以受控方式引导它们返回地球开辟了新的可能性——猎鹰9号的大部分部件可以重复使用多达100次。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Truly environmentally friendly space travel is still some way off.","cn":"真正环保的太空旅行仍有一段路要走。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But we already have many of the technologies needed to start limiting its impact on our planet.","cn":"但我们已经拥有许多开始限制其对地球影响所需的技术。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Helping to look after a pet can facilitate numerous aspects of a child's emotional development.","cn":"帮助照顾宠物可以促进儿童情感发展的诸多方面。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Research shows that reading to a loyal and nonjudgmental companion, such as a dog or cat, can encourage reluctant readers to read aloud, which will in turn boost their self-confidence.","cn":"研究表明,向忠诚且不评判的伙伴(如狗或猫)朗读可以鼓励不愿意读书的孩子大声朗读,这反过来会增强他们的自信心。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Having a companion to talk to about their feelings can also help children feel secure and develop communication skills.","cn":"有一个可以倾诉感受的伙伴也能帮助儿童感到安全并发展沟通技能。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"A household pet can also cultivate a child's sense of responsibility as their parent explains the necessary processes of keeping their pet happy and healthy.","cn":"家庭宠物还可以培养儿童的责任感,因为家长会向他们解释保持宠物快乐和健康的必要过程。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"As a child matures, they can then take on more of the daily responsibilities, boosting their sense of independence.","cn":"随着儿童的成长,他们可以承担更多日常责任,增强独立感。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Pets also provide a fantastic subject for research and learning.","cn":"宠物还为研究和学习提供了绝佳的主题。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Parents can encourage their child to research their favourite pets at the library or during a supervised internet search.","cn":"家长可以鼓励孩子在图书馆或在监督下的网络搜索中研究他们喜爱的宠物。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Taking children along to the pet shop to buy food and supplies will support their cognitive development as their passion for learning flourishes.","cn":"带孩子去宠物店购买食物和用品将有助于他们的认知发展,因为他们对学习的热情会蓬勃发展。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"A child's physical development can benefit greatly from taking pets for walks in the fresh air.","cn":"带宠物在新鲜空气中散步可以极大地促进儿童的身体发育。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Even their fine-motor skills can be utilised in taking care of a beloved animal.","cn":"甚至他们的精细运动技能也可以在照顾心爱的动物时得到运用。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"When responsibilities are well paced and communicated, a child can benefit greatly from involvement in bringing up a happy and healthy pet.","cn":"当责任节奏得当且沟通良好时,儿童可以从参与养育一只快乐健康的宠物中受益匪浅。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"And of course, if a child doesn't have a pet in their own household, they can still benefit from all of the above when visiting a friend who does.","cn":"当然,如果孩子自己家里没有宠物,他们在拜访有宠物的朋友时仍然可以从上述所有方面受益。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"A new bill in the Ohio legislature would require state public colleges and universities to send prospective students a packet of information.","cn":"俄亥俄州立法机构的一项新法案将要求州立公立大学和学院向潜在学生发送一份信息包。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This would include costs of college, grants and scholarships.","cn":"其中将包括大学费用、助学金和奖学金。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"It would also include expected monthly loan payments and projected salary after college.","cn":"还将包括预期的月贷款还款额以及大学毕业后的预期薪资。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"State Representative Adam Mathews is one of the two legislators who proposed the bill.","cn":"州众议员Adam Mathews是提出该法案的两位立法者之一。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"He said it would give prospective students more information about what to expect once they graduate.","cn":"他表示，这将为潜在学生提供更多关于毕业后预期情况的信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"\"Putting that information in front of them will give them the best opportunity to match their skills and their dreams to what our schools can provide,\" said Mathews.","cn":"Mathews说：\"将这些信息呈现在他们面前，将使他们有最好的机会将自己的技能和梦想与我们学校所能提供的相匹配。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"He notes that the state can only regulate public institutions in this way, but he hopes private institutions in Ohio follow the lead of the state and post similar information.","cn":"\"他指出，州只能以这种方式监管公立机构，但他希望俄亥俄州的私立机构效仿州的做法并发布类似信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"He believes giving out this information will help Ohio's colleges and universities to be more competitive.","cn":"他相信，提供这些信息将有助于俄亥俄州的大学和学院提高竞争力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The information will highlight what a great value they have for their very reasonable cost.","cn":"这些信息将突显出它们以非常合理的成本提供了巨大的价值。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Ohio's schools are already competitive.","cn":"俄亥俄州的学校已经很有竞争力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The state attracts more undergraduate students than it sends to colleges out of state.","cn":"该州吸引的本科生数量超过了流失到州外大学的数量。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Many colleges and universities currently provide similar information on their websites.","cn":"许多大学和学院目前在其网站上提供类似信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This includes tuition, fees, graduation rates and more.","cn":"这包括学费、费用、毕业率等。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"But students need to search for the information.","cn":"但学生需要主动搜索这些信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This bill would require the universities and colleges to send a packet directly to students.","cn":"该法案将要求大学和学院直接向学生发送信息包。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2024-06-2","level":"CET6","exam":"2024_06_2","year":2024,"month":6,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2024年6月 六级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2024年6月 CET-6 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet6-2024-06-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I've just bought a new blender.","cn":"M: 我刚买了一台新搅拌机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: What's that?","cn":"W: 那是什么？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: A blender, you know, a machine that blends food.","cn":"M: 搅拌机，你知道，就是一种用来搅拌食物的机器。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Uh, yes, of course, the electric kitchen appliance.","cn":"W: 呃，知道，当然知道，就是那种电动厨房用具。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Exactly, this one is state-of-the-art.","cn":"M: 没错，这台是最先进的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I've been meaning to buy one for a while, and I did thorough research on which specific model to get.","cn":"我想买一台已经有一段时间了，而且还认真研究了到底该买哪个具体型号。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I read through maybe hundreds of online user reviews.","cn":"我大概看了上百条网上的用户评价。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Anyway, it's amazing.","cn":"总之，它太棒了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Really?","cn":"W: 真的吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What could be so special about it?","cn":"它到底有什么特别的？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I mean it's just a blender.","cn":"我的意思是，它不就是一台搅拌机吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Well, basically, it's just a very good one.","cn":"M: 嗯，基本上，它就是一台非常好的搅拌机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It feels heavy and sturdy and well made.","cn":"拿在手里感觉很重、很结实，做工也很好。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It also has lots of power and can easily cut and crush practically anything.","cn":"它的功率也很大，几乎什么东西都能轻松切碎、碾碎。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"This way, the soups and juices I make come out really fine and smooth, with no lumpy bits.","cn":"这样一来，我做出来的汤和果汁都特别细腻顺滑，没有结块。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Um, I see.","cn":"W: 嗯，我明白了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I've never thought of getting one myself.","cn":"我从来没想过自己也买一台。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It sounds like the kind of thing that, for me personally, I would rarely use.","cn":"听起来，这种东西对我个人来说应该很少会用到。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I've never had one before, and now that I do. I use it all the time. I make a fresh fruit juice in the morning, maybe not every morning, but three or four times a week, and it feels fantastic. It's a really healthy habit.","cn":"M: 我以前从来没有搅拌机，但现在有了以后，我一直在用。我早上会做新鲜果汁，也不是每天早上都做，但每周会做三四次，而且感觉特别棒。这真是个非常健康的习惯。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I can imagine that must feel quite satisfying.","cn":"W: 我能想象那一定很令人满足。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I can picture you getting all creative in the kitchen and trying out a multitude of different ingredient combinations, and it's obviously going to be healthier than buying packaged juice from a supermarket.","cn":"我都能想象你在厨房里发挥创意，尝试各种各样的食材组合，而且这显然会比从超市买包装果汁更健康。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: It's so much healthier. It's not even close. Did you know that store-bought juice is like 10% sugar?","cn":"M: 健康多了，根本不是一个级别的。你知道吗，商店里买的果汁含糖量大约是百分之十？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Right, so then you bought it for the health benefits?","cn":"W: 好吧，所以你买它主要是为了健康方面的好处？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Mostly yes.","cn":"M: 主要是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Basically, it allows me to have a more varied diet with a far wider assortment of nutrients, because it's not only fruit in my morning juices you see.","cn":"基本上，它让我能拥有更加多样化的饮食，摄入种类丰富得多的营养，因为你看，我早上的果汁里可不只是水果。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I can also throw in vegetables, nuts, yogurts, cereals, anything that tickles my fancy.","cn":"我还可以加蔬菜、坚果、酸奶、谷物，任何我喜欢的东西都行。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Today we have a very interesting guest. Mr. Thomas Benjamin Grimm, the mayor of Berkton, is here to talk about his job and responsibilities overseeing this charming village. Mr. Grimm, thank you for being here.","cn":"W: 今天我们请到了一位非常有趣的嘉宾。伯克顿的市长托马斯·本杰明·格里姆先生来到这里，和我们谈谈他的工作，以及负责管理这个迷人的村庄所承担的责任。格里姆先生，感谢您今天来到这里。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Thank you for having me.","cn":"M: 谢谢您的邀请。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I'd like to start by stating the obvious.","cn":"W: 我想先从一个显而易见的事实说起。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Berkton has become one of the most popular tourist destinations in the country, and this has happened under your watch.","cn":"伯克顿已经成为全国最受欢迎的旅游目的地之一，而这一切都是在您的任期内发生的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Just how did you achieve this?","cn":"您究竟是如何做到的？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: The achievement belongs to all the residents of Berkton.","cn":"M: 这项成就属于伯克顿的所有居民。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It was a shared effort where everybody pitched in for the communal good.","cn":"这是大家共同努力的结果，每个人都为公共利益贡献了自己的力量。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: But how did this change happen?","cn":"W: 但这种变化是如何发生的呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"In about 10 years, Berkton has gone from a relatively unheard-of sleepy village to a must-see destination.","cn":"大约10年的时间里，伯克顿从一个相对默默无闻、寂静沉睡的村庄，变成了一个必游之地。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Yes, the change has truly been remarkable. Berkton was always fortunate to be endowed with such a beautiful natural allure. The Ambury Hills above the village remain untouched by human development, and the Sonora Valley just below it is equally stunning. The transformation commenced in a town hall meeting in spring 2008 over 10 years ago now, when an overwhelming majority of neighbors voted in favor of \"Motion 836\". This legislative proposal essentially set out to harmonize the aesthetic appearance of all the houses in Berkton. The idea was that if all the properties looked a certain way with shared design features, then a village as a whole would look more beautiful. And it worked.","cn":"M: 是的，这种变化确实非常显著。伯克顿一直很幸运，拥有如此美丽的自然风光。村庄上方的安布里山丘仍未受到人类开发，而下方的索诺拉谷同样美不胜收。这场转变始于十多年前，也就是2008年春天的一次市政厅会议。当时，绝大多数居民投票赞成了“第836号动议”。这项立法提案的核心目标，是让伯克顿所有房屋的外观风格协调统一。这个想法是，如果所有房产都采用某种统一的外观和共同的设计元素，那么整个村庄看起来就会更加美丽。事实证明，这确实奏效了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: It certainly did.","cn":"W: 确实如此。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm looking now at a before-and-after photo, and the change is truly remarkable.","cn":"我现在正在看一张改造前后的照片，这种变化真的非常显著。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's hard to believe it's the same place.","cn":"很难相信这是同一个地方。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And how do the neighbors feel now?","cn":"那么，居民们现在对此有什么感受呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Great pride, I would say.","cn":"M: 我想，他们感到非常自豪。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: But what about the multitudes of visitors now crowding the streets?","cn":"W: 但现在有成群的游客挤满街道，这又怎么样呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Is everyone happy about that?","cn":"大家对此都感到满意吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: The tourists we receive are a blessing, as they have completely revitalized our local economy.","cn":"M: 我们迎来的游客是上天的恩赐，因为他们让我们的地方经济彻底恢复了活力。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Every visitor is warmly welcome.","cn":"每一位游客都会受到热情欢迎。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Researchers in the US have created a remote-controlled robot that is so small it can walk on the top of a US penny.","cn":"美国研究人员研制出一种遥控机器人，小到可以在一枚美国一美分硬币的顶部行走。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"In research published in the journal Science Robotics, a team at Northwestern University said the crab-like robot is 0.5mm wide.","cn":"在《科学机器人学》杂志发表的一项研究中，西北大学的一个团队表示，这种蟹状机器人宽度仅为0.5毫米。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Researchers described it as the smallest-ever remote-controlled walking robot.","cn":"研究人员称，这是迄今为止最小的遥控行走机器人。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The tiny robot can bend, twist, crawl, walk, turn, and even jump without the use of complex hardware or special power.","cn":"这种微型机器人无需复杂的硬件或特殊动力，就能弯曲、扭转、爬行、行走、转弯，甚至跳跃。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The engineers said this is because the robot is powered by the elastic property of its body.","cn":"工程师表示，这是因为机器人依靠其身体的弹性特性驱动。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"To construct the robot, the researchers used a shape-memory alloy material that transforms to its remembered shape when heated.","cn":"为了制造这种机器人，研究人员使用了一种形状记忆合金材料，这种材料受热后会恢复到其记忆中的形状。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Using a laser, the team is able to heat the robot at specific parts of its body, causing it to change shape.","cn":"团队利用激光加热机器人身体的特定部位，使其发生形变。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"As the robot deforms and goes back to its original shape, it creates movement from one place to another.","cn":"当机器人变形并恢复到原来的形状时，就会产生从一个地方移动到另一个地方的运动。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"\"Because these structures are so tiny, the rate of cooling is very fast,\" project lead Professor John A.","cn":"项目负责人约翰·A·罗杰斯教授说：“由于这些结构非常微小，冷却速度非常快。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Rogers said.","cn":"事实上，缩小这些机器人的尺寸可以使它们运行得更快。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"\"In fact, reducing the sizes of these robots allows them to run faster.\"","cn":"”"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"While the research is still in the exploratory phase, the team believes that technology could lead to micro-sized robots that can perform practical tasks in tightly confined spaces. \"You might imagine micro-robots as agents to repair or assemble small structures or machines in industry or as surgical assistants to clear clogged arteries, to stop internal bleeding, or to eliminate cancerous tumours—all in minimally invasive procedures,\" Rogers said.","cn":"尽管这项研究仍处于探索阶段，但团队相信，这项技术可能促成能够在极其狭窄空间内执行实际任务的微型机器人。罗杰斯说：“你可以设想，微型机器人可作为执行者，在工业领域维修或组装微小的结构或机器；也可以作为手术助手，在微创手术中清除堵塞的动脉、止住内出血或消除癌性肿瘤。”"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"I don't want to boast or anything, but I have always considered myself something of an elite sleeper.","cn":"我不想自夸什么的，但我一直认为自己算得上是睡眠精英。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Given the opportunity, I will sleep for marathon stretches, and can doze through the most extreme situations.","cn":"只要有机会，我就会一睡数小时，甚至在最极端的情况下也能打瞌睡。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"On one very rough ferry crossing, on the route to the Isles of Scilly, for example, my traveling companion spent the entire 3-hour-ride throwing up in the bathroom, while I dozed happily on a plastic chair.","cn":"例如，在一次前往锡利群岛的航线上，渡轮经历了一段非常颠簸的航程，我的同伴在整个3小时的旅途中都待在卫生间里呕吐，而我却惬意地坐在塑料椅上打盹。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Unfortunately, it has come to my attention that I am not an elite sleeper after all.","cn":"遗憾的是，我最近才意识到自己终究算不上睡眠精英。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It seems I am just lazy, because elite sleepers are defined as the approximately 3 percent of the population who are biologically programmed to need less sleep than the rest of us.","cn":"看来我只是懒，因为睡眠精英的定义是：约占总人口3%、在生理上注定比我们其他人需要更少睡眠的人。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"According to a study that came out in March, elite sleepers have rare genetic changes, which means they can sleep fewer hours than mere mortals, without any risk of cognitive decline.","cn":"根据一项于3月公布的研究，睡眠精英存在罕见的基因变化，这意味着他们睡眠时间少于普通人，却不会面临认知能力下降的风险。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It may not be possible to change your own genes, but can you train yourself to need less sleep?","cn":"改变自己的基因或许不可能，但你能训练自己减少睡眠需求吗？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Is there a non-biological way to reach elite sleeper status?","cn":"有没有一种非生物学的方法可以成为睡眠精英？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"I have spent the past year trying to answer that question.","cn":"过去一年里，我一直在努力回答这个问题。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Not for fun, I should add, but because having a baby has severely disrupted my sleep, for which I still have a great passion.","cn":"需要补充说明的是，这并不是为了好玩，而是因为生孩子严重打乱了我的睡眠，而我至今仍然非常热爱睡觉。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For a while, I assumed I'd be forced to become one of those people who jump out of bed at the crack of dawn.","cn":"有一段时间，我以为自己不得不变成那种天一亮就从床上跳起来的人。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"After a year of tough scientific study, however, I have discovered being forced to get up early in the morning is very different from being an early bird.","cn":"然而，经过一年的艰苦科学研究，我发现，被迫早起与早起的人是两回事。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"If you read an article about a controversial issue, do you think you'd realise if it had changed your beliefs?","cn":"如果你读了一篇有关争议性问题的文章，你认为自己会意识到它是否改变了你的信念吗？"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"No one knows your own mind like you do—it seems obvious that you would know if your beliefs had shifted.","cn":"没有人比你更了解自己的想法——你似乎理所当然会知道自己的信念是否发生了变化。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"And yet a new paper in the Quarterly Journal of Experimental Psychology suggests that we actually have very poor awareness of our own belief change, meaning that we will tend to underestimate how much we've been swayed by a convincing article.","cn":"然而，《实验心理学季刊》发表的一篇新论文表明，我们实际上很难觉察到自己的信念变化，这意味着我们往往会低估自己受一篇有说服力的文章影响的程度。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The researchers recruited over two hundred undergraduates across two studies and focused on their beliefs about whether physical punishment of kids is an effective form of discipline.","cn":"研究人员在两项研究中招募了两百多名本科生，重点考察他们对于体罚孩子是否是一种有效管教方式的看法。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The students reported their initial beliefs about whether physical punishment is an effective way to discipline a child on a scale from \"1\" completely disbelieve to \"9\" completely believe.","cn":"学生们首先在“1”（完全不相信）到“9”（完全相信）的量表上报告自己对于体罚是否是管教孩子的有效方式的初始看法。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Several weeks later they were given one of two research-based texts to read: each was several pages long and either presented the arguments and data in favour of physical punishment or against it.","cn":"几周后，他们被安排阅读两篇基于研究的文章中的一篇：每篇文章都有数页之长，分别陈述支持或反对体罚的论据和数据。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"After this, the students answered some questions to test their comprehension and memory of the text.","cn":"读完后，学生们回答了一些问题，以测试他们对文章内容的理解和记忆。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Then, the students again scored their belief about whether physical punishment is effective or not.","cn":"随后，学生们再次对自己认为体罚是否有效进行评分。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Finally, the researchers asked them to recall what their belief had been at the start of the study.","cn":"最后，研究人员要求他们回忆研究开始时自己的看法。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The students' belief about physical punishment changed when they read a text that argued against their own initial position.","cn":"当学生们读到一篇主张反对其最初立场的文章时，他们对于体罚的看法发生了变化。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Crucially, the memory of their initial belief was shifted in the direction of their new belief—in fact, their memory was closer to their current belief than their original belief.","cn":"关键在于，他们对自己初始看法的记忆也朝着新看法的方向发生了偏移——事实上，他们记忆中的初始看法比起原先的看法，更接近当前的看法。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The more their belief had changed, the larger this memory bias tended to be, suggesting the students were relying on their current belief to deduce the initial belief.","cn":"他们的看法变化越大，这种记忆偏差通常也越大，这表明学生们可能是在依靠当前的看法来推断最初的看法。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The memory bias was unrelated to the measures of how well they'd understood or recalled the text, suggesting these factors didn't play a role in memory of initial belief or awareness of belief change.","cn":"记忆偏差与他们对文章的理解程度或回忆程度无关，这说明这些因素并未影响他们对初始看法的记忆，也未影响他们对信念变化的觉察。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The researchers concede that this research was about changes to mostly moderate beliefs—it's likely the findings would be different in the context of changes to extreme or deeply held beliefs.","cn":"研究人员承认，这项研究考察的是主要处于中等程度的信念变化——如果是在极端或根深蒂固的信念发生变化的情况下，研究结果很可能会有所不同。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"However, our beliefs on most topics are in the moderate range, and as we go about our daily lives reading informative material, these intriguing findings suggest we are mostly ignorant of how what we just read has updated and altered our own position.","cn":"然而，我们对大多数问题的看法都处于中等范围，而且当我们在日常生活中阅读信息性材料时，这些耐人寻味的发现表明，我们大多没有意识到刚刚读到的内容如何更新并改变了自己的立场。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"As the American population grows, so does the number of American moms.","cn":"随着美国人口增长，美国母亲的人数也在增加。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But, more than a century after Mother's Day became an official holiday, even as that number increases, the share of the American population who are mothers is at the lowest point in a quarter century.","cn":"但是，在母亲节成为法定节日一个多世纪之后，尽管这一人数不断上升，母亲在美国总人口中所占的比例却处于四分之一世纪以来的最低点。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"It's frequently noted that fertility rates are falling sharply in richer countries.","cn":"人们经常注意到，较富裕国家的生育率正在急剧下降。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But the less-observed consequence of this trend is that the decline in births can also mean a decline in motherhood in America.","cn":"然而，这一趋势一个较少被关注的后果是，出生人数减少也可能意味着美国母亲人数的减少。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"According to my analysis of data from the Census Bureau, the decline of American motherhood is real, occurring very quickly, and may continue for some time yet.","cn":"根据我对人口普查局数据的分析，美国母亲人数的下降确实存在，发生得非常迅速，而且可能还会持续一段时间。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Not only are moms making up less of the population, but their characteristics are changing too, and in a way that might be linked to their proportional decline.","cn":"母亲不仅在总人口中所占的比例越来越低，她们的特征也在发生变化，而且这种变化可能与她们比例上的下降有关。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Moms today tend to be older than in the past.","cn":"如今的母亲往往比过去年长。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Just looking at recent years, the change in age-specific birth rates has been drastic.","cn":"仅从近几年来看，不同年龄段的生育率变化就十分显著。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In just the past few years, the peak childbearing age range for American women has advanced from that of 25-29 to that of 30-34.","cn":"就在过去几年中，美国女性生育高峰年龄段已从25至29岁推移到30至34岁。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Meanwhile, childbearing among women under 20 has fallen by half or more, while childbearing among women 35 and older is rising.","cn":"同时，20岁以下女性的生育率下降了一半甚至更多，而35岁及以上女性的生育率正在上升。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"One positive consequence of this age shift is that a larger proportion of new mothers are economically prepared to raise children.","cn":"这一年龄变化带来的一个积极后果是，新生母亲中有更大比例在经济上已做好抚养孩子的准备。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Less positively, however, many women find that, as they age, they can't have as many kids as they would like.","cn":"然而，不那么积极的是，许多女性发现，随着年龄增长，她们无法生育自己希望拥有的那么多孩子。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Plus, having children later in life can increase the risk of health complications.","cn":"此外，晚年生育还会增加出现健康并发症的风险。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"These finer points aside, one major consequence of the older-moms trend is that fewer years of a woman's life are spent as a mother.","cn":"撇开这些更细致的问题不谈，母亲年龄增长趋势的一个主要后果是，女性一生中作为母亲度过的年数减少了。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This means that, at any given time, a larger share of women, and thus of the whole population, will report not having children in government surveys.","cn":"这意味着，在任何特定时点，接受政府调查的女性中，以及因此在全部人口中，报告自己没有孩子的人所占比例都会更高。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In other words, later motherhood means less motherhood.","cn":"换句话说，晚育意味着较少的母亲经历。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Even as motherhood rates decline, Mother's Day, of course, will endure.","cn":"即使母亲比例正在下降，母亲节当然仍将延续下去。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In fact, despite the demographic shift, retail spending on the holiday appears to be rising.","cn":"事实上，尽管人口结构发生了变化，这一节日的零售消费似乎正在增加。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"It is hard to say if Mother's Day spending is rising more than one would expect, given that the American population keeps growing, but one factor might be that the proportion of women who are the mothers of adult children is rising.","cn":"很难说母亲节消费的增长是否超出了美国人口持续增长这一因素所能带来的预期，但其中一个原因可能是，成年子女的母亲在女性中的比例正在上升。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"And those adult children may spend more generously when it comes to celebrating the moms they no longer live with.","cn":"而这些成年子女在庆祝那些已经不再与自己共同生活的母亲时，可能会更加慷慨。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Since NASA published a paper in 1989 claiming that houseplants can soak up pollution and toxic chemicals, businesses and homeowners have increasingly invested in greenery to help clean their air.","cn":"自美国国家航空航天局（NASA）于1989年发表一篇论文，声称室内植物能够吸收污染物和有毒化学物质以来，企业和房主越来越多地投资于绿植，以帮助净化空气。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But, a new analysis suggests it could actually take more than 1,000 plants per square meter to gain a benefit any greater than simply opening a couple of windows.","cn":"然而，一项新的分析表明，要获得任何超过简单打开几扇窗户所能带来的益处，实际上可能需要每平方米摆放超过1000株植物。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The problem lies in the fact that NASA conducted their tests in sealed containers that do not simulate the conditions in most people's homes or offices. The space agency was primarily concerned about keeping the air fresh for astronauts cut off in biospheres or space stations and helping to combat \"sick building syndrome\", which had become a problem due to the super insulated and energy efficient offices of the late 1970s. By the early 1980s, workers regularly complained of skin rashes, sleeplessness, headaches, and allergies as they breathed in toxic chemicals from paints and plastics.","cn":"问题在于，NASA是在密封容器中进行测试的，而这种环境并不能模拟大多数人家中或办公室的实际情况。该航天机构主要关注的是如何为被隔绝在生物圈或空间站中的宇航员保持空气清新，以及帮助应对“病态建筑综合征”。由于20世纪70年代末的办公室采用了高度隔热且节能的设计，这种综合征逐渐成为一个问题。到了20世纪80年代初，员工经常抱怨出现皮疹、失眠、头痛和过敏症状，因为他们吸入了来自油漆和塑料的有毒化学物质。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"NASA found that certain plants could remove chemicals from the air, and even today, garden centers recommend the plants for air cleaning properties.","cn":"NASA发现，某些植物能够去除空气中的化学物质，直到今天，园艺中心仍会因这些植物具有净化空气的功效而予以推荐。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"However, a new evaluation of dozens of studies spanning 30 years found that houseplants in a normal environment have little impact.","cn":"然而，一项对历时30年、涵盖数十项研究的新评估发现，在正常环境中，室内植物的影响微乎其微。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In fact, natural ventilation is far better at cleaning the air.","cn":"事实上，自然通风在净化空气方面要有效得多。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The researchers also calculated the clean air delivery rate for plants in the studies they analyzed and found that the rate at which plants disperse the compounds was well below the usual rate of air exchange in a normal building, caused by the movement of people coming and going, opening doors and windows.","cn":"研究人员还计算了所分析研究中植物的清洁空气输送率，发现植物分散这些化合物的速率远低于普通建筑通常的空气交换速率；后者是由人员进出以及开关门窗等活动造成的。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Many of the studies did show a reduction in the concentration of volatile organic compounds over time, which is likely why people have seized on them to praise the air purifying virtues of plants.","cn":"许多研究确实显示，挥发性有机化合物的浓度会随着时间推移而降低，这可能就是人们抓住这一点来赞美植物净化空气功效的原因。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But the researchers' calculation showed it would take 10 to 1,000 plants per square meter of floor space to compete with the air cleaning capacity of a building's air handling system or even just a couple of open windows in a house.","cn":"但研究人员的计算表明，要与建筑空气处理系统，甚至住宅中仅仅打开几扇窗户的空气净化能力相匹敌，每平方米地面面积需要摆放10至1000株植物。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In contrast, NASA's sealed experiment recommended one pot plant per 100 square feet.","cn":"相比之下，NASA的密封实验建议每100平方英尺摆放一盆植物。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This is certainly an example of how scientific findings can be misleading or misinterpreted over time.","cn":"这无疑说明，科学发现可能会随着时间推移而产生误导或被误解。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But it's also a great example of how scientific research should continually reexamine and question findings to get closer to the ground truth of understanding what's actually happening.","cn":"但这也很好地体现了科学研究应当不断重新审视并质疑已有发现，从而更加接近对实际情况的真实理解。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2024-12-1","level":"CET6","exam":"2024_12_1","year":2024,"month":12,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2024年12月 六级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2024年12月 CET-6 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet6-2024-12-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: OK then, this here is your yearly performance review. You've been with the company for 3 years and under my direct supervision for the past 12 months. Your report is mostly good. But there are a couple of issues we must discuss. The report is yours to take with you. We'll go through the main points together now. And you can come through it in greater detail later. Do you have any questions before we start?","cn":"M: 好吧，这份是你的年度绩效评估。你已经在公司工作三年了，过去十二个月一直由我直接负责。你的报告总体不错，但有几个问题我们必须讨论一下。这份报告你可以带走。现在我们先一起过一遍重点，之后你可以再仔细看看。开始之前，你有什么问题吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: No, sir.","cn":"W: 没有，先生。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I'll get straight to it then.","cn":"M: 那我就直说了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It is evident that you are a hard worker.","cn":"很明显，你工作很努力。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"You are punctual and industrious.","cn":"你很守时，也很勤奋。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Furthermore, you have strong analytical skills and attention to detail.","cn":"此外，你有很强的分析能力，而且注重细节。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The company, myself included, is happy with your productivity and overall performance.","cn":"公司，包括我在内，都对你的工作效率和整体表现感到满意。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Thank you.","cn":"W: 谢谢。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I appreciate the recognition.","cn":"能得到这样的认可，我很感谢。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Do you agree, then, with this depiction so far?","cn":"M: 那么，到目前为止，你同意这份描述吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Yeah, it's a little simplistic perhaps.","cn":"W: 嗯，也许有点过于简单了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But that's to be expected from this kind of evaluation.","cn":"不过，这种评估大概就是这样。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Sure.","cn":"M: 当然。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Would you want to add anything?","cn":"你想补充些什么吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Your comments can be added to the report if you wish.","cn":"如果你愿意，我们可以把你的意见加到报告里。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Oh, there's no need.","cn":"W: 哦，没必要。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's a flattering portrayal really.","cn":"说真的，这份描述已经很恭维我了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Thank you, though.","cn":"不过还是谢谢你。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: OK.","cn":"M: 好。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"This leads me to the not-so-good part.","cn":"这就说到不太好的部分了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"This mostly centers around one behavioral aspect—your ability to work with others.","cn":"主要涉及一个行为方面的问题，也就是你与他人合作的能力。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I see.","cn":"W: 我明白了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Yes.","cn":"M: 是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"As you already know, over the last several months, there have been some complaints raised about your communication style.","cn":"你也知道，过去几个月里，有人对你的沟通方式提出了一些投诉。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Of course, we already had like three meetings about this.","cn":"W: 当然了，我们已经为这件事开过大概三次会了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Look, all I'm going to say is that it was never my intention to offend anyone.","cn":"听着，我只想说，我从来没打算冒犯任何人。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Simply put, I don't like to write long emails, because, frankly, I think they're a waste of time.","cn":"简单来说，我不喜欢写很长的邮件，因为坦白说，我觉得那是在浪费时间。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Conciseness is efficiency.","cn":"简洁就是效率。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I feel that writing long emails hurts that same productivity you praised me for just a minute ago.","cn":"我觉得写长邮件会损害你刚才还在称赞的那种工作效率。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And I already apologized if anyone was offended.","cn":"如果有人觉得受到了冒犯，我也已经道过歉了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But to be perfectly honest, I think anyone who was offended was being a little too sensitive.","cn":"但说句完全坦诚的话，我认为那些感到被冒犯的人有点太敏感了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: So tell me, why do you wish to study medicine?","cn":"M：那么请告诉我，你为什么想学医？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I've always wanted to be a doctor.","cn":"W：我一直都想成为一名医生。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I come from a small town where healthcare was never the best.","cn":"我来自一个医疗条件始终不太好的小镇。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And I think that had a profound effect on me.","cn":"我觉得这对我产生了深远的影响。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"As a child, I remember thinking how great it would be to serve the community and cure people!","cn":"小时候，我记得自己常常想，要是能服务社区、治愈病人，那该多好啊！"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: What other people or events in your life have shaped your interest in becoming a doctor?","cn":"M：你生活中的其他哪些人或哪些事情促使你产生了成为医生的兴趣？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Well, that's hard to say.","cn":"W：这个很难说。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I would certainly say my parents have been a key factor.","cn":"我当然会说，我的父母是一个关键因素。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"They always pushed me to study hard.","cn":"他们总是督促我努力学习。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And I certainly wouldn't be here without their support.","cn":"要不是他们的支持，我肯定不会坐在这里。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I guess I was also immensely fortunate to have good teachers and friends around me.","cn":"我想，我也非常幸运，身边有优秀的老师和朋友。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"At the end of the day, I've always been surrounded by a positive environment conducive to my working hard and pursuing my dreams.","cn":"总的来说，我一直处在一个积极向上的环境中，这个环境促使我努力学习、追逐梦想。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Is there any medical branch that you would like to specialize in?","cn":"M：你有没有想专攻的医学分支？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I haven't decided yet.","cn":"W：我还没决定。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's still early days.","cn":"现在还早。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"However, if I had to say, internal medicine.","cn":"不过，如果一定要说的话，我想选内科。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Why internal medicine?","cn":"M：为什么是内科？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I know it's no picnic.","cn":"W：我知道这可不是件轻松的事。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But I find it the most intriguing, because it covers so much and ties together so many other specialties.","cn":"但我觉得内科最有意思，因为它涉及的范围很广，还把许多其他专科联系在了一起。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Thank you.","cn":"M：谢谢。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Now I'd like to address your academic history and projected grades.","cn":"现在我想谈谈你的学业经历和预期成绩。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"We like to think of ourselves as a prestigious institution with a highly competitive and promising student body.","cn":"我们愿意把自己看作一所享有盛誉的院校，拥有一批竞争力强、前途光明的学生。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"As you know, to get into our programmes, you need at least 85% score in the entrance exam.","cn":"你知道，要进入我们的课程，入学考试至少要考到85%。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Do you think you can attain this?","cn":"你觉得自己能达到这个分数吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I think so.","cn":"W：我想可以。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Yes.","cn":"是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I'm looking at your school grades now and I'll be honest. It's a bit of a mixed bag. You do get top grades here and there, but you are not very… Shall we say \"consistent\"? I see no problem in making you a conditional offer, but consider yourself warned, our entrance exam is, to use your own words, no picnic.","cn":"M：我现在正在看你的在校成绩，我直说吧，情况有好有坏。你有些科目成绩确实很优秀，但你并不是很……怎么说呢，“稳定”？我不介意有条件地录取你，但你要做好心理准备，我们的入学考试，用你自己的话说，可不是件轻松的事。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Logging into your email account can sometimes feel like trying to hack into the Pentagon.","cn":"登录电子邮箱账户有时感觉就像试图入侵五角大楼。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"If you follow all of the guidelines, you need to use a different password for every one of your accounts; use an incomprehensible variety of letters, numbers, and symbols; sign up for two-step verification; and change every password every time one of them is compromised.","cn":"如果遵循所有指南，你需要为每个账户使用不同的密码；使用由字母、数字和符号组成的令人难以理解的组合；注册两步验证；并且每当其中一个密码遭到泄露时，就更改所有密码。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"More often than not, you then have to choose photos that include a street sign, as this apparently provides solid evidence to your computer that you are, in fact, a human being.","cn":"更常见的是，接下来你还必须选择包含街道标志的照片，因为这显然能向电脑提供确凿证据，证明你确实是人类。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It's no small wonder most of us forget our passwords more often than our keys.","cn":"难怪我们大多数人忘记密码的次数比忘记钥匙的次数还多。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Now a new peer-reviewed study by researchers at Aalto University in Finland is attempting to figure out why we forget our passwords in order to help put an end to this frustrating phenomenon.","cn":"如今，芬兰阿尔托大学的研究人员开展了一项新的同行评议研究，试图弄清我们为何会忘记密码，以帮助终结这一令人沮丧的现象。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Their findings suggest that how likely you are to remember your password has less to do with the password itself and more to do with how often you anticipate using it.","cn":"他们的研究结果表明，你记住密码的可能性有多大，与密码本身的关系较小，而更多地取决于你预期使用它的频率。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Which is to say: you are far more likely to remember a complicated password if you know you'll frequently be using it to log into an account than you are to remember a simple password for an account that you don't expect to log into very often.","cn":"也就是说，如果你知道自己会经常使用一个复杂密码登录某个账户，那么你记住它的可能性要远高于记住一个简单密码的可能性，后者所对应的账户是你预计不会经常登录的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The researchers advise websites to include more of an incentive for users to log in more often in order to help them remember their secret codes.","cn":"研究人员建议网站为用户更频繁登录提供更多激励，以帮助他们记住自己的密码。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Four years ago, Jenny Weiner was in a fitness slump. She wanted to improve her physical and mental health. However, her workouts lacked intensity without a proper training programme to follow. When she went to the gym, her daily ritual predominantly involved easy exercise options like jogging; she avoided more formidable exercises like lifting weights. A personal trainer who might push her was out of the question. The extravagant cost was just unaffordable. She then discovered the fitness phone app Slimmeretics. To use the app, you first input your profile about your previous training experiences and preferences, as well as your desired goals. A virtual coach then uses that information to suggest a personalised training regime. After the workout, the app's artificial intelligence software system gives feedback from Ms. Weiner and its other 53 million users around the world to adjust future training sessions. Now Ms. Weiner finds the workouts exciting. This is because no two are ever the same. As a result, the app has helped her to lose more than 25 kilograms. The app's mathematical approach can arrange a more meticulous workout schedule. This has led to optimal results. However, some experts think that apps cannot replace human personal trainers. An app cannot understand human behavior. It will not comprehend that there are competing interests outside of health and fitness. Additionally, a human trainer can add compassion to the workout. He can also make exercise fun and sustainable. Trainers can monitor whether a person is doing exercises correctly. This can safeguard against injuries. An app cannot perceive such subtleties.","cn":"四年前，Jenny Weiner 的身体状况正处于低谷。她希望改善自己的身心健康。然而，由于没有适当的训练计划可供遵循，她的锻炼缺乏强度。她去健身房时，每天的锻炼主要都选择慢跑之类的轻松项目；而像举重这样更具挑战性的运动，她则避而远之。请一位能够督促她的私人教练更是不可能的事，因为高昂的费用实在负担不起。后来，她发现了健身手机应用 Slimmeretics。要使用这款应用，首先需要输入个人资料，包括以往的训练经历和偏好，以及期望达到的目标。随后，虚拟教练会利用这些信息为用户制定个性化的训练方案。锻炼结束后，这款应用的人工智能软件系统会根据 Weiner 女士以及全球其他5300万名用户的反馈，调整未来的训练安排。如今，Weiner 女士觉得锻炼很令人兴奋。这是因为每次锻炼都不尽相同。因此，这款应用帮助她减重超过25公斤。该应用采用数学方法，可以安排更加细致周密的锻炼计划，从而取得最佳效果。然而，一些专家认为，应用程序无法取代人类私人教练。应用程序无法理解人类行为，也无法明白除了健康和健身之外，人们还会面临其他相互竞争的需求。此外，人类教练可以在锻炼中融入关怀，也能让运动变得有趣且可持续。教练可以监督一个人是否正确完成动作，从而防止受伤。应用程序无法察觉这些细微之处。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"All societies are held together by seven universal moral rules, which include deferring to superiors and respecting the property of others, Oxford University has concluded.","cn":"牛津大学得出结论，所有社会都由七条普遍的道德规则维系在一起，其中包括服从上级和尊重他人财产。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Although many cultures are moving towards more liberal, less hierarchical organizations, the new research suggests that traditional power structures and basic values of charity and brotherhood are the cornerstones of successful societies.","cn":"尽管许多文化正朝着更加自由、等级制度更弱的组织形式发展，但这项新研究表明，传统的权力结构以及慈善和兄弟情谊等基本价值观，才是成功社会的基石。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The huge study of 60 different cultures around the world found that all communities operate under seven basic moral codes.","cn":"这项针对世界各地60种不同文化的大规模研究发现，所有群体都遵循七项基本的道德准则。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Those universal rules are: help your family, help your group, return favors, be brave, defer to superiors, divide resources fairly, and respect the property of others.","cn":"这些普遍规则是：帮助家人，帮助群体，回报他人的帮助，勇敢，服从上级，公平分配资源，以及尊重他人的财产。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The character traits held for every kind of community, be they traditional hunter gatherers or advanced civilizations, helping to uphold civilized society and foster social cooperation, researchers found.","cn":"研究人员发现，无论是传统的狩猎采集者群体，还是先进文明，各类社会都重视这些品格；这些品格有助于维护文明社会并促进社会合作。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"\"Everyone everywhere shares a common moral code,\" said Dr. Oliver Scott Curry, lead author and senior researcher at Oxford.","cn":"“每个地方的每个人都拥有共同的道德准则，”牛津大学首席作者兼高级研究员奥利弗·斯科特·柯里博士说，“这七条道德规则之所以在不同文化中都具有普遍性，是因为人们面临着相同的社会问题。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"\"These seven moral rules appear to be universal across cultures, because people face the same social problems.","cn":"即便其中一些品格看起来属于右翼或保守立场，例如服从权威，左翼人士仍然会表现出对某个群体的忠诚，以及对某个人或某种事物的服从。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Even if some of these traits look right-wing or conservative, for example, deferring to authority, left-wing people will still have a group loyalty and deference to someone or something.","cn":"这表明，真正将我们联结在一起的因素多于分裂我们的因素。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This shows there really is more that unites us than divides us.\"","cn":"”"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The study published in Current Anthropology is the largest and most comprehensive and widespread survey of morals ever conducted and aimed to find out whether different societies had different versions of morality. The team accessed the world's best archives to analyze accounts from more than 600 sources of 60 societies around the world. They found that the seven rules were considered morally good in all societies and were observed across all continents, religions and politics. However, some communities valued certain rules more highly than others. Dr. Curry hopes that this research helps to promote mutual understanding between people of different cultures and appreciation of what we have in common and how and why we differ. Co-author professor Harvey Whitehouse said social scientists should now set about testing the theory in the field, rather than relying on old data. \"This study was based on historical descriptions of cultures around the world,\" he said. \"These descriptions were made independent of and prior to the theory we're testing. In future, if social scientists are serious about testing theories of morality, they will need to gather new data, more systematically, out in the field.\"","cn":"这项发表于《当代人类学》的研究，是迄今开展的规模最大、最全面且覆盖范围最广的道德调查，旨在 выяс明不同社会是否拥有不同版本的道德观。研究团队查阅了世界上最权威的档案资料，分析了来自世界各地60个社会的600多份资料记载。他们发现，在所有社会中，这七条规则都被视为合乎道德的准则，并且在各大洲、各种宗教和不同政治体系中都得到遵守。不过，一些群体对某些规则的重视程度高于其他规则。柯里博士希望，这项研究能够促进不同文化之间的相互理解，帮助人们认识到彼此的共同点，以及我们存在差异的方式和原因。合著者哈维·怀特豪斯教授表示，社会科学家现在应当着手在实地检验这一理论，而不是依赖旧数据。他说：“这项研究建立在对世界各地文化的历史描述之上。这些描述是在独立于我们所检验的理论、且早于该理论提出的情况下形成的。今后，如果社会科学家认真对待道德理论的检验，就需要在实地以更加系统的方式收集新数据。”"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"When it comes to food, color is money.","cn":"说到食品，颜色就是金钱。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Food companies know that better color gives better prices, so they ensure that their products are attractive in color to bolster earnings.","cn":"食品公司深知，颜色越好，价格就越高，因此它们会确保产品的色泽具有吸引力，以增加收益。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Oranges, for example, have to meet specific color standards.","cn":"例如，橙子必须符合特定的色泽标准。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"And oranges are just the beginning.","cn":"而橙子还只是开始。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"There are color standards for foods including French fries, tomatoes, pumpkins, olives, honey and cherries.","cn":"包括炸薯条、西红柿、南瓜、橄榄、蜂蜜和樱桃在内的食品，都有相应的色泽标准。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The attention to color is for good reason.","cn":"人们之所以如此重视颜色，是有充分理由的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"For all the talk of the tongue, our eyes really might be the most important part of the eating experience.","cn":"尽管人们总是在谈论舌头，但我们的眼睛实际上可能是饮食体验中最重要的部分。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"A great number of our brain functions are dedicated to processing vision, while only a percent or two is given over to taste faculties, and the result is that color actually changes how we taste food.","cn":"我们大脑的大量功能都用于处理视觉信息，而分配给味觉功能的只有百分之一或百分之二，其结果是，颜色确实会改变我们品尝食物时的感受。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Scientists have demonstrated many times the importance of color to taste. In a 1980s study, for example, test participants were asked to name the flavor of the beverage they were drinking without being able to see that beverage. Only one in five was able to identify it as orange. But when they were allowed to see what they were drinking which was orange in color, each of them identified the orange flavor. And when a drink that was lime flavor was colored orange, nearly half of respondents identified the flavor of the beverage as orange. None made that mistake when the beverage was green in color. What's happening when someone fails to identify the flavor of a beverage they can't see or that has an abnormal color? Is it that participants can't discern what the flavor is, and so rely on visual cues? Or does color actually change the experience of taste? The key to these questions is the effect of color on expectation. The brain makes predictions using color. These predictions rely on expectations that come from experience. Research shows that we're all born liking sweet things and desire to eat them, but we aren't born knowing what the sweet things we crave look like. So we need to learn this over time. The brain gets information from the environment. And we learn, for example, that fruits go from green and sour to red and ripe and sweet. Thus, if we see a green berry, we equate its color with a sour taste, and just looking at a red fruit will activate our expectations that it will taste sweet and delicious.","cn":"科学家多次证明了颜色对味觉的重要性。例如，在20世纪80年代的一项研究中，实验参与者被要求说出所饮用饮料的味道，但他们无法看到饮料本身。只有五分之一的人能够辨认出那是橙子味。然而，当他们可以看到自己所饮用的饮料，而饮料呈橙色时，每个人都辨认出了橙子味。当一杯青柠味饮料被染成橙色时，近一半的受访者将饮料的味道辨认为橙子味。而当饮料呈绿色时，没有人犯这样的错误。当一个人无法辨认出自己看不见的饮料，或颜色异常的饮料的味道时，究竟发生了什么？是因为参与者无法分辨出它是什么味道，所以依赖视觉线索吗？还是颜色确实改变了味觉体验？这些问题的关键在于颜色对预期的影响。大脑会利用颜色作出预测，而这些预测依赖于来自经验的预期。研究表明，我们生来就喜欢甜食，也渴望食用甜食，但我们并不是天生就知道自己渴望的甜食看起来是什么样子。因此，我们需要随着时间的推移逐渐学会这一点。大脑从环境中获取信息。例如，我们会了解到，水果会从绿色、酸涩变成红色、成熟和甜美。因此，如果我们看到一颗绿色的浆果，就会将其颜色与酸味联系起来；而仅仅看到一个红色的水果，就会激活我们对其味道甜美可口的预期。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Searching for meaning is something many of us experience throughout our lives.","cn":"寻找意义是我们许多人一生都会经历的事情。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"For some, this meaning is religious, some political and some interpersonal.","cn":"对一些人来说，这种意义是宗教上的；对一些人来说，是政治上的；对另一些人来说，则是人际关系方面的。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And having a sense of meaning can bring us happiness.","cn":"而拥有意义感能够带给我们幸福。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"A new study looks at the relationship between meaning and happiness in the context of financial resources. Rhea Catapano from the University of Toronto and colleagues find meaning is a far weaker predictor of happiness for rich people than poorer people, suggesting economic resources can impact how we experience meaning. The team analysed data from over 500,000 people across 123 countries. The first study used data from a daily poll of US residents collected between 2013 and 2015. Well-being was tracked using measures of positive affect—whether, during the day before they were surveyed, participants had smiled or laughed a lot or experienced a lot of happiness. Meaning was measured through a daily \"purpose index\", which explored the extent to which participants felt that they like what they do every day and are motivated to achieve their goals. Finally, income levels were assessed. The results showed that the correlation between meaning and happiness was strongest among those in lower income brackets. But as income levels increased, the correlation became weaker. The second study looked at worldwide data. Happiness was measured using the same questions as in the first study, while meaning was measured using the single question: \"Do you feel your life has an important purpose or meaning?\" Again, the strength of the relationship between meaning and happiness depended on participants' income: meaning had a greater influence on happiness for those on lower incomes compared to those in higher brackets. In the final study, French participants indicated the extent to which they felt they led a purposeful and meaningful life and how much they considered themselves a happy person. Finally, rather than using specific income brackets, they placed themselves on a \"social ladder\", representing where they stand in society with regard to wealth, education, and career. The results from the study duplicated those of the first two.","cn":"一项新研究考察了在财务资源背景下意义与幸福之间的关系。多伦多大学的里娅·卡塔帕诺及其同事发现，对于富裕人群而言，意义是幸福感的预测因素，其作用远弱于对较贫困人群的作用，这表明经济资源可能会影响我们体验意义的方式。研究团队分析了来自123个国家的50多万人的数据。第一项研究使用了2013年至2015年间收集的美国居民每日民意调查数据。研究人员通过积极情绪指标追踪幸福感，即调查前一天，参与者是否曾多次微笑或大笑，或体验到很强的幸福感。意义感则通过每日的“目标指数”进行测量，该指数考察参与者在多大程度上觉得自己喜欢每天所做的事情，并且有动力实现自己的目标。最后，研究人员评估了收入水平。结果显示，意义与幸福之间的相关性在收入较低的人群中最强。但随着收入水平提高，这种相关性逐渐减弱。第二项研究考察了全球数据。幸福感采用与第一项研究相同的问题进行测量，而意义感则通过一个单一问题进行测量：“你是否觉得自己的生活具有重要的目标或意义？”同样，意义与幸福之间关系的强弱取决于参与者的收入：与收入较高的人群相比，意义对低收入人群幸福感的影响更大。在最后一项研究中，法国参与者表明了自己在多大程度上觉得过着有目标且有意义的生活，以及他们在多大程度上认为自己是一个幸福的人。最后，他们没有按照具体收入阶层进行划分，而是将自己置于一架“社会阶梯”上，以代表自己在社会中就财富、教育和职业而言所处的位置。该研究的结果与前两项研究的结果一致。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"So overall, meaning and happiness had a stronger relationship in those with fewer resources than those with more.","cn":"总的来说，资源较少的人群中，意义与幸福之间的关系比资源较多的人群更强。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This might be the case because rich individuals have more access to other sources of happiness—many of which will be external, like lack of stress or community.","cn":"这可能是因为富裕人士更容易获得其他幸福来源，其中许多来源是外部的，例如较少的压力或社区支持。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Thus, a focus on an internal sense of satisfaction, purpose or meaning is less important.","cn":"因此，对内在满足感、目标感或意义感的关注就没有那么重要了。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2024-12-2","level":"CET6","exam":"2024_12_2","year":2024,"month":12,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2024年12月 六级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2024年12月 CET-6 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2024/cet6-2024-12-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Hi, Alan.","cn":"W: 嗨，艾伦。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Sorry for not calling you back sooner.","cn":"抱歉没能早点给你回电话。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"You said on the phone you had something you needed to discuss with me?","cn":"你在电话里说有件事想和我讨论？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Well, to get right down to it, I'm having second thoughts about my major.","cn":"M: 好吧，直说了吧，我开始重新考虑自己的专业了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"With my family situation getting more complicated and the end of my university education nearing, persisting with Art History just doesn't seem the right choice.","cn":"随着家里的情况变得越来越复杂，而我也即将结束大学学业，坚持学艺术史似乎已经不是正确的选择了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Alan, in the last 3 years, I have heard nothing but how passionate you are about the Art History programme.","cn":"W: 艾伦，过去三年里，我听到的全都是你对艺术史专业有多么热情。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"You often told fellow classmates how fabulous the instructors were and that you finally felt accepted.","cn":"你经常告诉同学们这里的老师有多么出色，还说自己终于有了归属感。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What would cause you to abandon it?","cn":"究竟是什么让你想放弃它？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: My father's current financial situation has helped me realize that a more financially viable employment opportunity is not necessarily a bad thing.","cn":"M: 我父亲目前的经济状况让我意识到，选择一个经济上更可行的就业机会未必是件坏事。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Art History nourishes my soul, but does nothing to put food on my plate.","cn":"艺术史滋养了我的心灵，却无法解决我的温饱问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: What about all the work opportunities I discussed with you last month?","cn":"W: 那我上个月和你谈过的那些工作机会呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Have you gone to those places of business to investigate whether any legitimate positions might be available for someone with your background?","cn":"你有没有去那些公司了解一下，看看是否有适合你这种背景的人担任的正规职位？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Ah, well…","cn":"M: 啊，这个嘛……"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Look, Alan, if your heart is set on working in the art industry, you need to be more assertive and start talking with people.","cn":"W: 听我说，艾伦，如果你一心想在艺术行业工作，就得更加主动，开始和人交流。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Networking is key if you want to become a celebrity in the world of museums and galleries.","cn":"如果你想成为博物馆和画廊界的名人，人脉是关键。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Time is a very precious commodity right now.","cn":"M: 现在时间非常宝贵。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"My social life does not exist.","cn":"我的社交生活根本不存在。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I can barely keep up with my studies and thesis is due by the end of this year.","cn":"我连学业都勉强应付得来，而论文要在今年年底前提交。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"When can I find time to research jobs when I have so much to do as it is?","cn":"我已经有这么多事情要做，哪儿还有时间去研究工作呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: What you do now will determine your future options.","cn":"W: 你现在所做的一切将决定你未来的选择。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Now is the optimum time to put forth your best effort.","cn":"现在正是拿出最大努力的最佳时机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I will take what you said into consideration.","cn":"M: 我会考虑你说的话。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The advice is much appreciated.","cn":"非常感谢你的建议。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Have you decided yet what your end-of-semester business project will be on?","cn":"M：你决定好学期末的商业项目要做什么了吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yes.","cn":"W：决定了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"How about you?","cn":"你呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Yes. Go on. You go first.","cn":"M：我也决定了。你先说吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I am going to do it about beef.","cn":"W：我打算做牛肉方面的项目。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Beef?","cn":"M：牛肉？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yeah, beef.","cn":"W：对，牛肉。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm going to design a business case study for a cow farm that supplies beef for the domestic market.","cn":"我打算为一家向国内市场供应牛肉的养牛场设计一份商业案例研究。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, that sounds very interesting and original.","cn":"M：听起来确实很有意思，也很有新意。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Wherever did you get that idea?","cn":"你到底是怎么想到这个点子的？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I don't know. It just came to me, I guess. But think about it. Beef consumption has been rising strongly over the past 20 years. As the economy continues to grow, consumer demand is expected to continue to increase for the foreseeable future. And currently, most of the beef is imported, which brings with it added fees. So why not raise cattle here?","cn":"W：我也不知道。我想大概就是突然想到的吧。不过你想想，过去20年来，牛肉消费量一直在大幅增长。随着经济持续发展，预计在可预见的未来，消费者的需求还会继续增加。而且目前大部分牛肉都是进口的，这还会带来额外的费用。所以，我们为什么不在这里养牛呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Of course.","cn":"M：当然可以。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Makes perfect sense.","cn":"完全说得通。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"There's plenty of land out west.","cn":"西部有的是土地。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So, if done right, it should be very profitable to raise our own cattle.","cn":"所以，只要经营得当，自己养牛应该会非常赚钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Exactly.","cn":"W：没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Seriously, that sounds like a great idea.","cn":"M：说真的，这听起来是个很棒的主意。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You should genuinely look into it once we get our degrees.","cn":"等我们拿到学位后，你确实应该好好研究一下。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Thanks.","cn":"W：谢谢。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So, your turn now.","cn":"现在轮到你了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"What are you doing your case study on?","cn":"你的案例研究要做什么？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I was thinking about a car wash, but it now seems like such a boring notion after hearing your brilliant idea.","cn":"M：我原本在考虑洗车店，但听了你这个绝妙的主意后，我的想法现在显得太无聊了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That's cool.","cn":"W：这想法不错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I could see that working.","cn":"我觉得能行。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"After all, there's plenty of cars about and those aren't going away any time soon.","cn":"毕竟，车很多，而且短期内也不会减少。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"While many people don't care how their car looks, many other people do.","cn":"虽然很多人不在乎自己的车看起来怎么样，但也有很多人在乎。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You got yourself a vast and continual market.","cn":"这样一来，你就拥有了一个庞大而持续的市场。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Right.","cn":"M：对。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So the idea is a large self-cleaning car wash, but I mean really big and well-outfitted like they have in America.","cn":"所以我的想法是开一家大型自助洗车店，不过要像美国那种真正规模很大、设备齐全的洗车店。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I was thinking of having it cater to high-end consumers in large cities.","cn":"我考虑让它面向大城市里的高端消费者。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It could charge a profitable markup by offering just a bit more technical equipment and professional service than competitors.","cn":"只要比竞争对手多提供一些技术设备和专业服务，就可以收取有利可图的溢价。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Increased television time for young children has long been linked with poorer progress in some areas of development.","cn":"长期以来，幼儿看电视时间增加一直与其在某些发展领域进步较差有关。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"One possible way to counter those negative effects is talking while watching the screen.","cn":"抵消这些负面影响的一种可能方式是在观看屏幕时进行交谈。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"As a new study suggests, the more parents engaged in conversation with preschoolers during TV time, the more likely those children were to have higher curiosity levels when they reached kindergarten.","cn":"一项新研究表明，父母在电视时间与学龄前儿童进行的对话越多，这些儿童进入幼儿园时表现出较高好奇心水平的可能性就越大。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"This was particularly true for children with socioeconomic disadvantages.","cn":"对于处于社会经济劣势的儿童而言，这一点尤其明显。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"\"Our findings reinforce the importance of parent conversation to promote early childhood development and curiosity,\" said lead author Prachi Shah at University of Michigan Health C.S. Mott Children's Hospital. Researchers assessed hours of daily television exposure and frequency of parent-screen-time conversation among 1,500 preschoolers, and then measured early childhood curiosity in kindergarten. The study specifically focused on curiosity levels, which are associated with enhanced learning and higher academic achievement in reading and math at kindergarten, and behavioral-developmental benefits, especially for children from families with lower socioeconomic status. While many young children are now growing up with digital media exposure through mobile devices like tablets and phones, television remains a dominant screen activity, accounting for 72% of all screen time. TVs are in 98% of all homes, keeping television exposure a relevant developmental context in young children.","cn":"密歇根大学健康中心C.S.莫特儿童医院的首席作者普拉奇·沙阿说：“我们的研究结果进一步证明，父母的对话对于促进幼儿早期发展和好奇心十分重要。”研究人员评估了1500名学龄前儿童每天接触电视的时长，以及父母在屏幕使用期间与孩子交谈的频率，随后测量了这些儿童进入幼儿园时的早期好奇心。该研究特别关注好奇心水平，因为好奇心与幼儿园阶段更强的学习能力、更高的阅读和数学学业成就，以及行为和发展方面的益处相关，尤其是对来自社会经济地位较低家庭的儿童而言。如今，许多幼儿通过平板电脑和手机等移动设备接触数字媒体，但电视仍然是主要的屏幕活动，占全部屏幕使用时间的72%。所有家庭中有98%拥有电视，这使电视接触仍然是幼儿发展中一个重要的环境因素。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Excessive media exposure, including television, can displace exploratory activities such as play and parent-child interactions, which are believed to be key to cultivating curiosity in kids. \"Our findings suggest the importance of parents finding opportunities to foster conversational exchanges in daily routines with their young children—including while watching television,\" Shah said.","cn":"过度接触媒体，包括看电视，可能会挤占游戏和亲子互动等探索性活动，而这些活动被认为是培养儿童好奇心的关键。沙阿说：“我们的研究结果表明，父母应当在日常生活中寻找机会与幼儿进行对话交流，包括在观看电视时进行交流。”"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Humans are aspirational goal-seeking beings.","cn":"人类是有抱负、追求目标的存在。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Each of us, according to research, has an inborn drive to acquire.","cn":"研究表明，我们每个人天生都具有获取的驱动力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The \"dark side\" of this drive to acquire is being mindlessly driven to possess more and more \"things\" and to socially compare our \"stuff\" with all the stuff other people have in their lives.","cn":"这种获取驱动力的“阴暗面”，在于不假思索地驱使自己拥有越来越多的“东西”，并将自己的“财物”与他人生活中拥有的一切进行社会比较。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"So the question is, how do we ensure we tap into our drive to acquire in positive ways that will benefit our well-being?","cn":"因此，问题在于，我们该如何确保以积极的方式运用这种获取驱动力，从而增进自身的幸福感？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"One way is to become more intentionally aspirational.","cn":"一种方法是更加有意识地树立抱负。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"To be intentionally aspirational includes consciously aspiring to be the person you need to be to succeed in your professional and personal life.","cn":"有意识地树立抱负，包括自觉追求成为一个能够在职业生活和个人生活中取得成功所需要成为的人。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It also includes consciously aspiring to acquire things in your life that will positively impact your sense of well-being.","cn":"这也包括自觉追求获得生活中那些能够积极影响你幸福感的事物。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"If you're not consciously, mindfully and intentionally harnessing this inborn drive to acquire, you might be mindlessly pursuing all the wrong things.","cn":"如果你没有有意识、专注而明确地驾驭这种与生俱来的获取驱动力，就可能会在不假思索地追求所有错误的事物。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"While your intentional aspirational goals will include pursuit of acquiring things that will increase your sense of well-being, they ought to also include goals to help other people in your various life roles.","cn":"虽然你有意识树立的抱负目标会包括追求获得能够提升幸福感的事物，但这些目标也应包括在你所承担的各种生活角色中帮助他人的目标。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Your intentional aspirational goals will also include striving to be your personal best—a person of \"good\" character, integrity, and trustworthiness.","cn":"你有意识树立的抱负目标还应包括努力做到最好的自己，成为一个具有“良好”品格、正直而值得信赖的人。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Think about this from a practical, rather than theoretical viewpoint.","cn":"请从实际而非理论的角度思考这一点。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"If you're not pursuing intentional aspirational goals, you have nothing to strive for.","cn":"如果你没有追求有意识树立的抱负目标，就没有任何目标可供努力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"If you have nothing to strive for, you're putting yourself in the dangerous position of simply drifting through life, and you will not be able to experience, live and enjoy all that life has to offer.","cn":"如果你没有任何目标可供努力，就会使自己处于一种危险境地，只是在生活中随波逐流，也就无法体验、生活并享受人生所能提供的一切。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It's revision time for exams and dissertations.","cn":"现在是准备考试和论文的复习阶段。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The pressure is on, so you want all the help you can get to aid your memory and raise your grades.","cn":"压力很大，因此你希望得到一切可能的帮助来增强记忆力、提高成绩。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"As a nutrition expert, I want to say that eating well can make a real difference to your revision regime—so what brain-boosting food and drink would I recommend?","cn":"作为一名营养专家，我想说，吃得健康能让你的复习安排产生显著不同，那么我会推荐哪些能增强大脑功能的食物和饮品呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Coffee can have numerous benefits.","cn":"咖啡有许多益处。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"However, while coffee may make you more alert, individuals can build up a tolerance, meaning this is short-lived.","cn":"然而，虽然咖啡可能会让你更加警觉，但人们会逐渐产生耐受性，这意味着这种效果是短暂的。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Coffee can also increase blood sugar and eventually cause lack of focus and energy.","cn":"咖啡还会升高血糖，最终导致注意力和精力不足。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It's also worth noting that people react differently to coffee.","cn":"同样值得注意的是，人们对咖啡的反应各不相同。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Some people can drink it at midnight and go straight to sleep, whereas others get feelings of anxiety after a small amount.","cn":"有些人可以在午夜喝咖啡后直接入睡，而另一些人只喝少量咖啡就会感到焦虑。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Also remember that coffee from a coffee shop may be stronger than coffee made at home.","cn":"还要记住，咖啡店的咖啡可能比家里冲的咖啡浓。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"So stop drinking coffee by 2 pm and have a maximum of 2 cups of coffee a day, but be aware of your own reaction to it.","cn":"因此，下午两点后就不要再喝咖啡了，每天最多喝两杯，但要留意自己对咖啡的反应。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Whole grain foods will ward off hunger.","cn":"全谷物食品可以防止饥饿。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Examples include porridge and whole wheat bread.","cn":"例子包括粥和全麦面包。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Combining whole grain foods with protein will help keep your blood sugar levels balanced, which is essential for mood and concentration.","cn":"将全谷物食品与蛋白质搭配食用，有助于保持血糖水平平衡，而这对情绪和注意力至关重要。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Berries and nuts are a convenient and nutritious snack.","cn":"浆果和坚果是方便又有营养的零食。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Blueberries, like many dark colored fruits and vegetables, can slow down brain damage and age-related decline.","cn":"蓝莓和许多深色水果、蔬菜一样，可以减缓大脑损伤和与年龄相关的衰退。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Frozen berries are also a good choice.","cn":"冷冻浆果也是不错的选择。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"They are usually cheap, last longer and don't lose their nutrients when frozen.","cn":"它们通常价格便宜、保存时间更长，而且冷冻后不会损失营养成分。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But flavored and coated nuts are less healthy as they contain added oil, salt, and sugar.","cn":"但调味坚果和裹层坚果不那么健康，因为其中含有额外添加的油、盐和糖。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Doctors often recommend taking vitamin supplements to top up on the nutrients you need.","cn":"医生经常建议服用维生素补充剂，以补充你所需的营养物质。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But I would say food should always come before supplements and the key to getting as many nutrients as possible is to eat a varied diet with lots of different colors such as frozen berries and dark green vegetables.","cn":"但我认为，食物始终应该优先于补充剂，而获得尽可能多营养的关键，是食用包含多种不同颜色食物的多样化饮食，例如冷冻浆果和深绿色蔬菜。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It's better to get everything you need from food and drink.","cn":"最好从食物和饮品中获取你所需要的一切。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"For example, oranges contain not only vitamin C which boosts the immune system, but also fiber and other components that you can't get packaged together in a tablet.","cn":"例如，橙子不仅含有能增强免疫系统的维生素C，还含有纤维和其他无法在一片药片中同时获得的成分。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Don't forget to drink a proper amount of water, which can boost attention by almost 25 percent and can elevate your mood as well.","cn":"别忘了饮用适量的水，这可以将注意力提高近25%，也能改善你的情绪。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Finally, don't skip meals.","cn":"最后，不要不吃饭。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Eating regularly will help keep blood sugar balanced and feed the brain with the fuel it needs.","cn":"规律进食有助于保持血糖平衡，并为大脑提供所需的能量。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The late Swedish academic Hans Rosling has identified a worrying trend: not only do many people across advanced economies have no idea that the world is becoming a much better place, but they actually even think the opposite.","cn":"已故瑞典学者汉斯·罗斯林发现了一个令人担忧的趋势：不仅许多发达经济体中的人们根本不知道世界正在变得越来越美好，实际上他们甚至认为情况恰恰相反。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This is no wonder, when the news focuses on reporting catastrophes, terrorist attacks, wars, and famines.","cn":"当新闻集中报道灾难、恐怖袭击、战争和饥荒时，这也就不足为奇了。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Who wants to hear about the fact that every day some 200,000 people around the world are lifted above the $2-a-day poverty line?","cn":"谁愿意听到这样的事实：世界各地每天约有20万人脱离每日2美元的贫困线？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Or that more than 300,000 people get access to electricity and clean water for the first time every day?","cn":"或者每天有超过30万人首次用上电并获得清洁饮用水？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"These stories in people in low-income countries simply don't make for exciting news coverage.","cn":"这些关于低收入国家民众的故事，确实难以成为令人兴奋的新闻报道内容。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But, as Rosling pointed out in his book Factfulness, it's important to put all the bad news in perspective.","cn":"但是，正如罗斯林在他的《事实》一书中指出的那样，重要的是要把所有坏消息放在整体背景下加以看待。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"While it is true that globalization has put some downward pressure on middle-class wages in advanced economies in recent decades, it has also helped lift hundreds of millions of people above the global poverty line.","cn":"诚然，近几十年来，全球化对发达经济体中产阶级的工资造成了一定的下行压力，但它也帮助数亿人脱离了全球贫困线。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"If we really care about global welfare, globalization is the only way forward to ensure that economic prosperity is shared among all countries and not only a select few advanced economies.","cn":"如果我们确实关心全球福祉，那么全球化就是确保经济繁荣惠及所有国家，而不仅仅是少数发达经济体的唯一前进道路。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"While some people glorify the past, one of the big facts of economic history is that until quite recently a significant part of the world population has lived under quite miserable conditions—and this has been true throughout most of human history.","cn":"虽然有些人美化过去，但经济史的一大事实是，直到相当晚近的时候，世界人口中仍有相当一部分生活在十分悲惨的条件下，而这在绝大部分人类历史时期一直如此。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"While there were many long-lasting ups and downs, like the Great Depression or the recent Great Recession, the constancy of the long-run growth rate is actually quite miraculous.","cn":"尽管长期以来经历了许多持续时间较长的起伏，例如大萧条或近期的大衰退，但长期增长率的稳定性实际上相当不可思议。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Low-income countries, including China and India, have been growing at a significantly faster pace in recent decades and are quickly catching up to the West.","cn":"包括中国和印度在内的低收入国家，近几十年来一直以明显更快的速度增长，并且正在迅速追赶西方。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"A 10% growth rate over a prolonged period means that income levels double roughly every seven years.","cn":"长期保持10%的增长率，意味着收入水平大约每七年翻一番。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"It is obviously good news if prosperity is more shared across the globe.","cn":"如果繁荣能够在全球范围内得到更广泛的共享，这显然是个好消息。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"While inequality within countries has gone up as a result of globalization, global inequality has been on a steady downward trend for several decades.","cn":"虽然全球化导致各国内部的不平等程度上升，但几十年来，全球不平等一直呈稳步下降趋势。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This is mostly a result of the improvement of hundreds of millions of people's living standards.","cn":"这主要是数亿人的生活水平得到改善的结果。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In fact, for the first time ever since the Industrial Revolution, about half of the global population can be considered middle class.","cn":"事实上，这是自工业革命以来，全球人口中约有一半首次可以被视为中产阶级。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"We all know that the sense of smell is powerful.","cn":"我们都知道，嗅觉的力量十分强大。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The delicious scent of bread, for example, can act like a time machine.","cn":"例如，面包的诱人香气就像一台时光机。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"One sniff can bring back a memory from many years ago.","cn":"闻一下，就能唤回许多年前的一段记忆。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Indeed, scent particles, in general, can revive memories that have been long forgotten.","cn":"事实上，气味分子通常能够唤醒那些早已被遗忘的记忆。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But why do smells sometimes trigger powerful memories, especially emotional ones?","cn":"但为什么气味有时会触发强烈的记忆，尤其是情感记忆呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The short answer is that the brain regions that handle smells, memories and emotions are linked.","cn":"简而言之，负责处理气味、记忆和情感的大脑区域彼此相连。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"A scent is a chemical particle that floats in through the nose and into the region of the brain responsible for smell, where the sensation is first processed into a form that the brain can read.","cn":"气味是一种化学微粒，它经由鼻腔飘入大脑中负责嗅觉的区域，在那里，这种感觉首先被处理成大脑能够读取的形式。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Brain cells then carry that information to the area of the brain where emotions are processed, and then to an adjacent area of the brain where learning and memory formation take place.","cn":"随后，脑细胞将这些信息传递到负责处理情感的大脑区域，再传递到相邻的、负责学习和记忆形成的大脑区域。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Scents are the only sensations that travel such a direct path to the emotional and memory centers of the brain.","cn":"气味是唯一能够沿着如此直接的路径到达大脑情感中枢和记忆中枢的感觉。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"That results in an intimate connection between emotions, memories and scents, which is why memories triggered by scents are experienced as more emotional than those triggered by sight or sound.","cn":"这就形成了情感、记忆和气味之间的密切联系，也正因如此，气味触发的记忆往往比视觉或听觉触发的记忆更具情感色彩。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Let's take a closer look at how those memories are activated.","cn":"让我们更仔细地看看这些记忆是如何被激活的。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Usually, when a person smells something that's connected to a meaningful event in their past, they'll first have an emotional response to the sensation and then a memory might follow.","cn":"通常，当一个人闻到某种与过去某个重要事件有关的气味时，他首先会对这种感觉产生情绪反应，随后记忆可能会浮现出来。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But sometimes, the memory doesn't come to the surface.","cn":"但有时，记忆并不会浮现。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The person might feel the emotion of something that happened in the past but won't remember what they experienced.","cn":"这个人可能会感受到过去发生的某件事所带来的情绪，却想不起自己当时经历了什么。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"What causes this baffling phenomenon?","cn":"是什么导致了这种令人困惑的现象？"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The explanation is context.","cn":"答案在于情境。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Imagine this scenario—a person is walking down the street smelling a scent that they first encountered decades ago, which activates an emotional response.","cn":"想象这样一个场景：一个人走在街上，闻到一种他几十年前第一次接触到的气味，这激活了他的情绪反应。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"If the person had first come across that smell in a very different context, it will be much more difficult to recover the associated memory, because the brain uses the context to give meaning to the information and find that memory.","cn":"如果这个人当初是在一个截然不同的情境中第一次闻到这种气味的，那么他就会更难回忆起与之相关的记忆，因为大脑会利用情境赋予信息意义，并找出那段记忆。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The special nature of memories brought back by scents notwithstanding, they have the same drawbacks as other memories.","cn":"尽管气味唤回的记忆具有特殊性，但它们也存在与其他记忆相同的缺陷。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"They aren't always accurate, and they can change over time.","cn":"它们并不总是准确的，而且会随着时间发生变化。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In fact, each time we remember something, that memory can become distorted.","cn":"事实上，每当我们回忆某件事时，那段记忆都有可能被扭曲。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But, because of the strong emotional associations these memories evoke, people who remember something due to a scent are often convinced that the memories are accurate, even when they aren't.","cn":"但是，由于这些记忆唤起了强烈的情感联系，那些因某种气味而回忆起某件事的人往往坚信自己的记忆是准确的，即使事实并非如此。"}]}];
